{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","hash":"99a58ed07a8aa9ebe5597fc5941c606a2e89f9af82202096996454c45bd59925","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm noticing `.detail-art` has no base styles outside the stage-specific rule — the quote variant sets background, color, column flex-direction, and gap, but without an explicit `display: flex` elsewhere, the flex-direction property likely has no effect.\n\nSo the quote art div ends up as a plain block with yellow background, a bold mark, and a \"Quote\" label span — which matches my ItemStageMedia styling. Now I'm checking whether the default art uses an `ink` class and whether `.ink` CSS actually exists, since mine uses `item.accent` directly without falling back to \"ink\" like the original seems to.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F2cckEwJFRk9khpExm26if","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-a1f541e8 && grep -n \"^\\.ink\\b\\|\\.ink {\\|\\.ink,\" src/App.css src/index.css; grep -rn \"accent:\" src/lib/*.ts | head -5","description":"Check ink class"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
