{"parentUuid":"22aba9e2-e3dc-40de-8006-004bc233843d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQWz7AiokmYu3Hr8guhK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm thinking through how to simulate a paste event in the renderer using a synthetic ClipboardEvent with DataTransfer items, generating test image bytes via canvas for PNG content so I can verify zoom/original swap behavior, and considering what's needed to produce a valid PDF byte source for similar testing.\n\nFor Article coverage I'm weighing whether fetching a real URL violates the network-use restriction, and realize the Article stage wasn't part of the original preview seed either—so I'm checking whether localSeedItems committed in this checkout already provides article content, or whether I'd need to paste a URL to trigger the fetch flow, which raises the network question again.\n\nI'm now considering spinning up a local HTTP server to serve a test article, since that avoids external network calls — though I'm unsure if the SSRF guard blocks localhost requests, so I'll test it and fall back to documenting Article as only verified through shared code paths if it's blocked. I also plan out the remaining full-app verification steps: creating a Space and confirming the Move-to-Space toggle updates membership, archiving an item from the view, resizing the window to check note editing at narrow heights, confirming the PDF viewer opens and closes with Escape, and checking that zooming an image swaps in the original file. Finally I'm sequencing the build steps — building the app in the current branch and also in the base worktree — before capturing before/after screenshots.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":868,"cache_read_input_tokens":230535,"output_tokens":1180,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":910},"server_too