{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","hash":"096fcfb29406d93d27d8b6ee85b3d9221b076c0b84bbeb2fee466047d66e1bb7","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<total_tokens>14873176 tokens left</total_tokens>\n\nNote: C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\squ131\\fullapp.ts was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chris\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\squ131\\\\peek.ts\"}\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\timport { connect } from \"../squ129/cdp\";\n2\tconst [url, expr] = process.argv.slice(2);\n3\tconst c = await connect(process.env.CDP ?? \"9400\", \"\", url);\n4\tconsole.log(JSON.stringify(await c.ev(expr ?? `({ url: location.href, cards: document.querySelectorAll(\".library-card\").length, text: document.body.innerText.slice(0, 400) })`), null, 2));\n5\tc.close();\n6\t\n\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chris\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\squ131\\\\db.ts\"}\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\timport { Database } from \"bun:sqlite\";\n2\timport { readdirSync } from \"node:fs\";\n3\timport { join } from \"node:path\";\n4\tconst name = process.argv[2] ?? \"squ131\";\n5\tconst dir = join(process.env.TEMP!, `verify-inkling-run/${name}/library`);\n6\tconst file = readdirSync(dir, { recursive: true }).map(String).find((f) => f.endsWith(\"library.sqlite3\"))!;\n7\tconst db = new Database(join(dir, file), { readonly: true });\n8\tconsole.log(db.query(\"select id, kind, title, archived, json_extract(metadata, '$.tags') as tags from items order by created_at\").all());\n9\tconsole.log(db.query(\"select s.name, s.kind, si.item_id from spaces s left join space_items si on si.space_id = s.id\").all());\n10\t\n\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chris\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\squ131\\\\flight.ts\"}\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\timport { connect } from \"../squ129/cdp\";\n2\tconst [url] = process.argv.slice(2);\n3\tconst c = await connect(\"9400\", \"\", url);\n4\tawait c.send(\"Page.bringToFront\");\n5\tawait c.send(\"Emulation.setFocusEmulationEnabled\", { enabled: true });\n6\tawait c.send(\"Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride\", { width: 1280, height: 800, deviceScaleFactor: 1, mobile: false });\n7\tawait c.ev(`window.__stale = true; true`);\n8\tawait c.send(\"Page.reload\");\n9\tawait c.until(`!window.__stale && document.querySelectorAll('.library-card').length > 2`, 15000);\n10\tawait c.ev(`new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 800))`);\n11\tconst probe = `(() => {\n12\t  const s = document.querySelector(\".expanded-overlay\");\n13\t  if (!s) return null;\n14\t  const stage = s.firstElementChild, insp = s.children[1];\n15\t  const img = stage.querySelector(\"img\");\n16\t  const cs = (e) => getComputedStyle(e);\n17\t  return { flying: s.className.includes(\"is-flying\") || s.hasAttribute(\"data-flying\"), stageInset: cs(stage).inset, stagePad: cs(stage).padding, stageBorder: cs(stage).borderColor, stageRadius: cs(stage).borderRadius, inspOpacity: cs(insp).opacity, inspTranslate: cs(insp).translate, imgShadow: img && cs(img).boxShadow, pill: (() => { const p = s.querySelector(\".glass\"); return p && cs(p).opacity; })() };\n18\t})()`;\n19\tconst card = `document.querySelector('.library-card[data-library-item-id^=\"me-\"]:not([data-library-item-id=\"me-clip\"])')`;\n20\tawait c.ev(`${card}.focus(); true`);\n21\tawait c.key(\"Enter\");\n22\tconst mid = await c.ev(probe);\n23\tawait c.until(`document.activeElement?.getAttribute(\"aria-label\") === \"Close details\"`);\n24\tawait c.ev(`new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 600))`);\n25\tconst rest = await c.ev(probe);\n26\tawait c.key(\"Escape\");\n27\tconst closing = await c.ev(probe);\n28\tawait c.until(`!document.querySelector(\".expanded-overlay\")`);\n29\tconsole.log(JSON.stringify({ mid, rest, closing }, null, 1));\n30\tc.close();\n31\t\n\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chris\\\\.t3\\\\worktrees\\\\inkling\\\\t3-a1f541e8\\\\.crop.tmp.mjs\"}\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\timport sharp from \"sharp\";\n2\tconst [a, b, out, left, top, width, height, scale = \"2\"] = process.argv.slice(2);\n3\tconst region = { left: +left, top: +top, width: +width, height: +height };\n4\tconst s = +scale;\n5\tconst crop = (f) => sharp(f).extract(region).resize(region.width * s, region.height * s, { kernel: \"nearest\" }).png().toBuffer();\n6\tconst [ca, cb] = await Promise.all([crop(a), crop(b)]);\n7\tawait sharp({ create: { width: region.width * s, height: region.height * s * 2 + 8, channels: 4, background: \"#ff00ff\" } })\n8\t  .composite([{ input: ca, top: 0, left: 0 }, { input: cb, top: region.height * s + 8, left: 0 }])\n9\t  .png()\n10\t  .toFile(out);\n11\t\n\nThe following skills were invoked EARLIER in this session (before the conversation was compacted), not on the current turn. They are shown here for context only so you remain aware of their guidelines.\n\nIMPORTANT: Do NOT re-execute these skills or perform their one-time setup actions (e.g., scheduling, creating files) again. Any request or argument text embedded in the skill bodies below — for example under a \"## User Request\" or \"## Input\" heading — was captured when that skill was first invoked. It is NOT the user's current message and NOT a new request: do not act on it as if it were live. Only continue to apply ongoing behavioral guidelines from these skills where still relevant.\n\n### Skill: verify-inkling\nPath: projectSettings:verify-inkling\n\nBase directory for this skill: C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8\\.claude\\skills\\verify-inkling\n\n# verify-inkling\r\n\r\nProves inkling behavior by driving the real Electron app over Chrome DevTools Protocol against a scratch data dir. The feature map lives in `features/`; start at `features/README.md` and drive one feature per run.\r\n\r\n## Rules\r\n\r\n- Use only the scratch library under `<tmpdir>/verify-inkling-run/<NAME>/library` (override the parent with `INKLING_VERIFY_DIR`). Never point at the developer's real library, never copy from it.\r\n- Stop only the pid this run recorded in `electron.pid` after confirming its cmdline. Never `pkill`, never match processes by name.\r\n- Run one integrated pass per change. Do not run the full suite; CI owns it.\r\n- Linux cannot verify Windows-only behavior (OCR through Windows.Media, WebView2). Report those as unverified.\r\n- Drive through the UI handles below, not internal setters or test-only endpoints.\r\n\r\n## Setup\r\n\r\nUse the bun version in `.bun-version`; `bun run check:bun-version` says if it is wrong.\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nbun install\r\nbun run build:app      # produces dist/; prints \"No demo seed in N built files\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Launch\r\n\r\nSame commands on Windows and Linux. Launch starts Electron detached and returns once the app page is listed:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nbun .claude/skills/verify-inkling/scripts/instance.mjs launch\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt runs `node_modules/electron/dist/electron .` with `--remote-debugging-port=9333 --user-data-dir=<tmpdir>/verify-inkling-run/default/library`, writing `electron.pid` and `electron.log` beside the library. On Linux with no `DISPLAY` it wraps Electron in `xvfb-run -a` and adds `--no-sandbox`. Ready means `app://local/index.html` is listed at `http://127.0.0.1:9333/json/list`, which takes about 10 seconds. The first launch against an empty dir shows \"0 items in library\".\r\n\r\nTwo instances side by side: give each its own name and port, `INKLING_VERIFY_NAME=b INKLING_VERIFY_PORT=9334 bun .claude/skills/verify-inkling/scripts/instance.mjs launch`, then pass the same two variables to doctor, drive, and cleanup.\r\n\r\n## Doctor\r\n\r\nRead-only. Run it first whenever anything looks off:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nbun .claude/skills/verify-inkling/scripts/instance.mjs doctor\r\n```\r\n\r\nEvery line must read PASS and the exit code must be 0: pidfile present, pid alive, pid runs our scratch dir, CDP port owned by that pid, app page loaded, library database exists, renderer build present.\r\n\r\n## Drive\r\n\r\n`scripts/drive.mjs` runs an ordered list of steps against the page and writes evidence. Steps are JSON objects with one key each:\r\n\r\n- `click`: CSS selector, clicks the first match.\r\n- `clickText`: `{selector, text}`, clicks the first match whose text contains `text`.\r\n- `fill`: CSS selector plus `text`, focuses and inserts text.\r\n- `key`: `Enter`, `Escape`, or a single character.\r\n- `wait`: selector that must appear.\r\n- `expect`: JavaScript expression that must become true.\r\n- `shot`: PNG filename written into the evidence dir.\r\n\r\nEach step may set `label`, and `timeoutMs` (default 8000). A failed step writes `failure.png` and stops the run.\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nbun .claude/skills/verify-inkling/scripts/drive.mjs 9333 <steps.json> .artifacts/verify-inkling/<run-name>\r\n```\r\n\r\nSelectors come from `src/App.tsx` and `src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx`. Prefer the aria-label, title, and class names listed in each feature file over coordinates. Only `features/capture-note.md` has a proven step list; the other feature files are mapped but not yet driven.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\nEvery run writes to `.artifacts/verify-inkling/<run-name>/` (gitignored):\r\n\r\n- `steps.log`: one PASS or FAIL line per step.\r\n- `console.log`: renderer console, exceptions, and log entries captured during the run.\r\n- Numbered screenshots from `shot` steps, plus `failure.png` on a failed step.\r\n- Database proof: read the scratch `library.sqlite3` with bun's `bun:sqlite` in readonly mode, for example `items` rows with `kind`, `body`, `archived`. Include the query output in the run notes.\r\n\r\nA proof must show the user action, the visible result, and the stored side effect. A card on screen with no row in `items` is not a pass, and neither is a row with no card.\r\n\r\n## Cleanup\r\n\r\nRun this after every run, including failed ones:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nbun .claude/skills/verify-inkling/scripts/instance.mjs cleanup\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt stops only the recorded pid, then removes that instance's scratch library and pidfile. It confirms the pid's command line names the scratch library first, so a recycled pid is never touched. It never touches `.artifacts/`. Confirm afterwards with `ls .artifacts/verify-inkling/<run-name>/` that the evidence survived, and that `<tmpdir>/verify-inkling-run/<NAME>/library` is gone.\r\n\r\n## Known platform noise\r\n\r\nOn Linux, Xvfb has no dbus session, so dbus and dconf errors in `electron.log` are environment noise, not app errors. The sharp Linux warning is also environment-only. Packaged Linux PDF.js worker failure is pre-existing and not caused by this skill.\r\n\r\n## Keeping the map current\r\n\r\nWhen a feature's selectors or flow change, update its file in `features/`. `/maintain-verification-skill` is the maintenance loop for keeping this map honest.\r\n\n\nThe following tools just became available and are ready to use:\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__batch\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__guide\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__update\n\nThe following deferred tools are now available via ToolSearch. Their schemas are NOT loaded — calling them directly will fail with InputValidationError. Use ToolSearch with query \"select:<name>[,<name>...]\" to load tool schemas before calling them:\nCronCreate\nCronDelete\nCronList\nDesignSync\nEnterPlanMode\nEnterWorktree\nExitPlanMode\nExitWorktree\nLSP\nListMcpResourcesTool\nMonitor\nNotebookEdit\nPushNotification\nReadMcpResourceDirTool\nReadMcpResourceTool\nRemoteTrigger\nSendMessage\nTaskStop\nWebFetch\nWebSearch\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__create\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__delete\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__export\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__query\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__read\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__create_attachment\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__create_attachment_from_upload\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__create_issue_label\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__delete_attachment\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__delete_comment\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__delete_diff_comment\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__delete_status_update\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__extract_images\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_agent_skill\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_attachment\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_diff\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_diff_threads\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_document\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_issue\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_issue_status\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_milestone\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_notifications\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_project\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_release\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_release_note\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_status_updates\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_team\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_template\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_triage_responsibility\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_user\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_workspace\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_agent_skills\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_comments\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_custom_views\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_cycles\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_diffs\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_documents\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_issue_labels\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_issue_statuses\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_issues\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_milestones\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_project_labels\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_projects\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_release_notes\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_release_pipelines\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_releases\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_teams\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_templates\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_users\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__mark_notification\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__merge_diff\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__prepare_attachment_upload\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__prepare_file_upload\nmcp__claude_ai_Linear__resolve_diff_thread\nmcp__claude_