{"parentUuid":"4f508423-5370-4aa0-9718-79a393461067","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQY1xP4D142EfMj3n1A2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's still a substantial amount of CSS left to migrate: global styles, brand mark, icon buttons, main content, paper components, text buttons, library header, toasts, note editor, onboarding, library stage, sidebar, and add menu. I'm planning to move the global styles like focus-visible, reduced motion, visually-hidden, and keyframes into index.css first.\n\nFor toasts, I'm thinking co-locating a toast.css next to the Toaster component makes sense since Sonner's styling works through data attributes rather than easily mapping to Tailwind classes. For the note editor, it's trickier since the styles target TipTap's generated ProseMirror content via descendant selectors, so keeping a co-located RichNoteEditor.css for that content feels right, similar to how reader styles work. I'm weighing whether to also convert the toolbar chrome to Tailwind for consistency with other components, though that adds conversion risk at this scale.\n\nThe editor also has embedded and focus modes with many variant overrides across roughly 570 lines of CSS, so converting the chrome to Tailwind would require conditional class logic. I want to move everything to a co-located RichNoteEditor.css and only convert the chrome if it's manageable, but first I should check whether the non-embedded `.note-editor` variant is even still used by looking at how RichNoteEditor is called elsewhere.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7368,"cache_read_input_tokens":102277,"output_tokens":861,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":732},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_i