{"parentUuid":"1b743716-8092-448e-8e00-b48052a944ca","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01MdQBeSb4mV21MCfDxbr5UX","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"325dccb3-5518-4785-9035-4a4136e5e7a4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:31:27.130Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
{"parentUuid":"325dccb3-5518-4785-9035-4a4136e5e7a4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQY4L6q168v18SM9rCda","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I notice index.css is fairly short, and that AddMenu.css and SegmentedControl.css remain as co-located CSS files from earlier work, which seems to be an accepted pattern in this codebase. Now I'm thinking through how to proceed concretely with this approach.\n\nFor index.css, I need to handle font imports (which must come after the @layer statement but alongside the tailwind imports due to CSS ordering rules), keep the focus-visible and reduced-motion globals unlayered to preserve their precedence behavior, and figure out the spin keyframe situation — since Tailwind v4 only emits theme keyframes when the corresponding animate utility is actually used, and we're using an arbitrary animate value rather than the built-in utility, I need to verify whether that keyframe will actually get generated.\n\nI'm also considering swapping `.visually-hidden` for Tailwind's `sr-only` utility, since the minor CSS differences (padding, margin, border-width) are irrelevant on genuinely hidden elements, and this seems safe to apply across usages like the hidden radio inputs in SegmentedControl.\n\nFinally I need to update the preflight comment in index.css once App.css is removed, since the rationale changes — preflight still shouldn't be enabled now because doing so would alter default styling on buttons, headings, and images across the app.\n\nFor the Surface.css comment on being unlayered, I'm reasoning through why that still matters: being unlayered lets `.glass` override Tailwind utility classes applied to the same element, so I want to rewrite that comment to reflect that the glass fill needs to win over any background a caller adds, though I'm not fully certain this behavior is actually relied upon anywhere and want to double check later.\n\nMoving into the Shell section, I'm mapping out which components need conversion — `.brand-mark` in MascotHomeSlot should become Tailwind classes, and `.icon-button` in ShortcutsDialog should probably use the existing IconButton component from the ui library instead of custom CSS.\n\nI'm also tracing where `.main-content`, `.is-sidebar-closed`, and `.library-header` get used across App.tsx and Sidebar.tsx, checking the CSS variables like `--main-pad-top` and `--stage-background` to see where they're referenced, and figuring out that the sidebar width override at the 1120px breakpoint needs to move into index.css while staying unlayered so it still wins over the theme layer's default. Then I'm noticing that the `.paper-*` accent classes used in useCapture, libraryItem, seed, and MascotFigure might actually be data-driven values stored as an `accent` field on items, meaning these class names need to be preserved rather than renamed since they could be persisted in the database.\n\nNow I'm checking whether accent strings are actually persisted or just derived at runtime in libraryItem.ts, since that determines whether I can safely rename them to Tailwind-style classes like `bg-blue-soft`. I'm also working through where the LiquidGlass component's CSS should live -- converting the canvas and content classes to inline Tailwind utilities in LiquidGlass.tsx, and figuring out how to express the library-stage-specific override for the glass canvas sizing.\n\nI'm reasoning through specificity: since App.css is being deleted, parent-scoped Tailwind arbitrary variants targeting the canvas hook class should still win over the component's own size-full utility because of selector specificity, so the hook classes need to stay on the elements even as Tailwind utilities get added alongside them.\n\nFor `.add-button`, the simplest move is relocating those rules into AddMenu.css since AddMenu already owns that component. For toasts, I'm considering wrapping sonner's Toaster in a dedicated component with its own co-located stylesheet, so I need to check how Toaster is currently used in App.tsx. For the note editor, I need to check whether RichNoteEditor's non-embedded mode and its `.note-editor` classes are actually still in use before deciding where those styles belong.\n\nGiven the dead code pruning I'm planning, and weighing the cost of converting the heavily mode-dependent chrome styles to Tailwind versus just keeping them as pruned co-located CSS, I'm leaning toward the simpler CSS approach since the task's actual requirement is just moving styles to their owners, not a full Tailwind conversion—the note editor's CSS is too tied to TipTap's descendant selectors to be worth converting anyway. Now I'm turning to onboarding, checking how its CSS file is imported and used by FirstRunOnboarding.\n\nI need to check whether the Breadcrumb component is used anywhere besides onboarding, since that determines whether its CSS can be folded into onboarding.css or needs to stay separate—there are nth-child animation selectors targeting breadcrumb elements that complicate converting it fully to Tailwind given unlayered CSS beats Tailwind's layered utilities on specificity. I'm also thinking through whether moving unlayered CSS into a separate file creates ordering risks across files when specificity ties occur.\n\nChecking the focus-visible selectors across note-editor and first-run styles confirms they're specific enough to avoid cascade conflicts regardless of file order, and the import order between index.css and App.css seems safe since co-located component CSS loads in module order anyway. I'm also noting that RichNoteEditor being lazy-loaded means its CSS becomes a separate chunk that Vite handles correctly for Electron, avoiding unstyled flashes — now I want to verify whether FirstRunOverlay is also lazy-loaded.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2218,"cache_read_input_tokens":125330,"output_tokens":3854,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3514},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2218,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3854,"cache_read_input_tokens":125330,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2218,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2218},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":37092,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgQY4KjVzrjRJLaB4BMHf","requestRef":"ea03b5a7-675c-4a87-87ea-ced439770dca","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5f0e9c53-0bfd-42ec-94cc-35de1cab8e42","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:31:27.128Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
