{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","hash":"55f5238b8fe82ca826668fc7c27ee57c1056806ccf92651d238bb0dba71abb04","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking that accent isn't persisted anywhere, then tracing how accent values map to Tailwind classes like \"bg-blue-soft\" that get picked up by content scanning and applied in LibraryCard via conditional class merging.\n\nSince both are utilities with the same property, class ordering is unreliable, so I'm deciding to explicitly fall back to a default surface class instead of relying on CSS cascade order. I'm also planning to convert the empty library-header section and main-content padding variables into Tailwind utility classes directly in App.tsx.\n\nStill verifying how Tailwind v4 orders max-width breakpoint variants to make sure the sidebar width overrides apply correctly at each screen size...\n\nI should check specificity concerns around `.main-content` references elsewhere in the codebase—only App.tsx and a Sidebar comment use it, so I'll update that comment to point to App's `<main>` instead, and verify whether CSS variables like `--main-pad-x` are referenced by ItemView or LibraryStage.\n\nNow I'm planning the index.css edits: where to add font imports relative to the existing Tailwind imports, and confirming how Tailwind v4's Vite plugin handles unlayered `@import` statements for fonts.\n\nActually, I'm reconsidering whether to import the fontsource CSS via Tailwind's resolver in index.css versus simply importing them as plain JS imports in main.tsx, which would be cleaner and avoid any import resolution quirks.\n\nDoing this makes knip see the fontsource packages as used, so I should remove them from the ignoreDependencies list in knip.json. I also need to rename visually-hidden to sr-only across six files, double-check the reduced-motion rule stays unlayered, and look at tidying the comment in Surface.css.\n\nI want to be careful with that comment, though — rather than asserting intent I don't fully know, I should check whether any elements actually combine a `glass` class with a `bg-` utility, since that would determine if moving the rule into a layer could break something.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"`accent` is runtime-only (never persisted), so the `paper-*` values can become Tailwind classes. Next I'll check how glass surfaces combine with utilities before deciding Surface.css's layer comment."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FbykjyKD1Q9AoDQduR9r1k","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-a1f541e8 && grep -rnE \"\\\"[^\\\"]*\\b(css-)?glass\\b[^\\\"]*\\\"\" src --include=*.tsx | grep -v \"liquid-glass\" | head -20; sed -n 245,262p src/features/library/LibraryCard.tsx","description":"Find glass class combos and LibraryCard accent use"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
