{"parentUuid":"b7e9a704-5c63-4c5f-bf88-0b4fec05d8c5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01CP4qqMAkckqwH9RGRpYeiH","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"bcb555ae-0545-424e-ba58-79f4c7a86f50","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:35:29.887Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
{"parentUuid":"bcb555ae-0545-424e-ba58-79f4c7a86f50","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQYNx2ZmA1hWdaYVAToq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Since the only caller always passes `embedded`, that prop is effectively always true, meaning the non-embedded styles are partially dead code. I'm checking whether `.note-editor-loading` actually shows up—it appears in the Suspense fallback when the body or editor is undefined, so those styles do apply.\n\nI'm weighing whether to simplify by removing the `embedded` prop entirely and folding its CSS overrides into the base rules, since the brief allows reducing unnecessary complexity, but merging the cascade by hand risks subtle mistakes given how focus-mode styles further override the embedded ones. I'm also deciding how much of the editor chrome—toolbar buttons, actions, content typography—should move to Tailwind versus staying as plain CSS, since TipTap's generated content elements likely need to remain in CSS regThe `note-editor-content` class comes from TipTap's editorProps attributes. I'm weighing whether to simplify by removing the unused `embedded` prop and folding its CSS overrides into the base rules, but merging cascades by hand risks errors since embedded overrides win by specificity and focus-mode overrides those too. I'm also deciding how much to convert to Tailwind—the TipTap-generated content styles (headings, lists, code blocks, links) need to stay as CSS, while the toolbar buttons and action buttons in JSX could potentially move to Tailwind classes.\n\nI'm leaning toward the pragmatic middle path: consolidate everything into a co-located RichNoteEditor.css, prune the dead non-embedded-only rules now that embedded is always true, and keep it parallel to how reader.css handles TipTap output. I'm going rule by rule to figure out which selectors are now dead given that embedded is always true, starting with the margin-top rule on `.note-editor` versus the embedded override that zeroes it out.\n\nChecking toolbar button specificity, I'm finding that min-width:30px from the base rule isn't actually overridden by the embedded selector's width:26px, so buttons may end up wider than intended — and the same min-width rule seems to bleed into heading-group buttons too, forcing them to 30px despite their own width:22px override.\n\nGiven this risk, pruning the CSS is too dangerous — I'll move the whole block verbatim (lines 326–898) into a new `RichNoteEditor.css` file and import it directly in the component, letting it load as a lazy CSS chunk. I'm confirming these note-editor classes aren't referenced anywhere else besides App.css and RichNoteEditor, so the move should be safe.\n\nChecking the loading timing: since Vite handles CSS deps for dynamic imports via its preload helper, the chunk's styles should load before the editor resolves, avoiding any flash of unstyled content, even under Electron's app:// protocol.\n\nNext I'm figuring out how to split the onboarding section (lines 900–1604) — likely into an `onboarding.css` file, while deciding whether Breadcrumb's CSS (used only by FirstRunOverlay) should move there too or get converted to Tailwind, keeping the `breadcrumb-list` hook class intact for its animation targeting.\n\nSince Breadcrumb.tsx owns that styling, I should check its actual implementation to see how the font-size override and list styling currently interact before deciding whether to extract a small `Breadcrumb.css` or convert it to Tailwind utilities.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1703,"cache_read_input_tokens":163190,"output_tokens":2572,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2416},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1703,"ephemeral_5m_input_to