{"parentUuid":"c7e6cc0d-ff2f-432e-85e0-7faca47cc6b6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQYR3M76anGsW4531GYJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm converting Breadcrumb to Tailwind while keeping the `data-slot=breadcrumb-list` attribute as a styling hook, and adjusting the onboarding CSS selectors to match that instead of the old class name.\n\nNow I'm deciding where the onboarding CSS file should live—placing it alongside the other onboarding components and importing it into FirstRunOverlay—then double-checking that the existing comments in that stylesheet are still relevant to keep.\n\nI'm going through each comment individually: keeping the one about SplitText's baseline quirk, keeping the note about the fixed type scale even though I'll fix its placement, trimming the explanation of the `--fr-dir` cross-file contract, and dropping the comments that just narrate design intent rather than explain a real constraint (like the headline/copy timing note and the \"keys taps down\" line). I'm keeping the comment about the negative margin trick since removing it would risk breaking the layout if someone touched it later.\n\nFor the remaining batch, I'm dropping the empty-frame label and the scan-beam narration, but keeping shortened versions of the dot-animation \"runs once, nothing repaints\" note and the KeptFloating transform-ownership explanations since those describe real cross-file dependencies. Now I'm planning to write a Python script that extracts each CSS/keyframe block by marker ranges and moves them into the appropriate files per the brief's instructions.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3358,"cache_read_input_tokens":164893,"output_tokens":2370,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1165},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_request