{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","hash":"f53d0762a090a9eb4b9767a7fb9cee964d3c13c141272b5ed72365a8fe3fb56d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm converting Breadcrumb to Tailwind while keeping the `data-slot=breadcrumb-list` attribute as a styling hook, and adjusting the onboarding CSS selectors to match that instead of the old class name.\n\nNow I'm deciding where the onboarding CSS file should live—placing it alongside the other onboarding components and importing it into FirstRunOverlay—then double-checking that the existing comments in that stylesheet are still relevant to keep.\n\nI'm going through each comment individually: keeping the one about SplitText's baseline quirk, keeping the note about the fixed type scale even though I'll fix its placement, trimming the explanation of the `--fr-dir` cross-file contract, and dropping the comments that just narrate design intent rather than explain a real constraint (like the headline/copy timing note and the \"keys taps down\" line). I'm keeping the comment about the negative margin trick since removing it would risk breaking the layout if someone touched it later.\n\nFor the remaining batch, I'm dropping the empty-frame label and the scan-beam narration, but keeping shortened versions of the dot-animation \"runs once, nothing repaints\" note and the KeptFloating transform-ownership explanations since those describe real cross-file dependencies. Now I'm planning to write a Python script that extracts each CSS/keyframe block by marker ranges and moves them into the appropriate files per the brief's instructions.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll convert Breadcrumb to Tailwind, with onboarding's selectors switched to its `data-slot` hooks, and move the onboarding and note-editor CSS to their owners."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016moopm73r3s3iZFEuPV5VX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-a1f541e8 && python - <<'EOF'\np='src/App.css'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nne_start=s.index('.note-editor {')\nfr_start=s.index('.first-run-overlay {')\nfr_end=s.index('/* LibraryStage.tsx.')\nnote=s[ne_start:fr_start].rstrip()+'\\n'\nonb=s[fr_start:fr_end].rstrip()+'\\n'\n# breadcrumb base styles move into Breadcrumb.tsx\nbc_start=onb.index('.breadcrumb-list {')\nbc_end=onb.index('@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {', bc_start)\nonb=onb[:bc_start]+onb[bc_end:]\nonb=onb.replace('.first-run-crumb .breadcrumb-list','.first-run-crumb [data-slot=\"breadcrumb-list\"]')\nreps=[\n('''} /* One type and control scale for every welcome screen, in stage pixels. The\n   stage itself scales with the window (FirstRunOverlay), so these never do. */\n/* Screens trade places sideways: --fr-dir is 1 going forward and -1 going\n   back, so the outgoing screen slips one way and the next arrives from the\n   other. Only opacity, translate and filter move, never the stage's scale. */\n''','''}\n/* The --fr-* scale is in stage pixels: FirstRunOverlay scales the stage with\n   the window, so never animate its scale. --fr-dir is 1 going forward and -1\n   going back. */\n'''),\n('''/* The copy under each headline rises in once the headline has mostly landed. */\n''',''),\n('''} /* Each key taps down once, in order, as if pressed. */\n''','''}\n'''),\n('''/* The empty frame the photo will arrive in. */\n''',''),\n('''/* Each dot lights up in turn, so the glow travels left to right and the\n   trail is left behind it. Runs once; nothing repaints afterwards. */\n''','''/* Runs once, so nothing repaints after the trail has lit. */\n'''),\n('''/* Mini inkling cards (the real card CSS is tuned for the grid, so these\n   borrow its colours and type at onboarding scale). KeptFloating sets each\n   card's transform; the layers differ only in how clear and how lifted. */\n''',''),\n('''/* The scan beam: a lit edge dragging a short trail down the receipt, once. */\n''',''),\n]\nfor a,b in reps:\n  assert a in onb, a[:40]; onb=onb.replace(a,b)\nopen('src/components/onboarding/onboarding.css','w',encoding='utf-8',newline='\\n').write(onb)\nopen('src/features/item-view/RichNoteEditor.css','w',encoding='utf-8',newline='\\n').write(note)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"/\\*\" src/components/onboarding/onboarding.css src/features/item-view/RichNoteEditor.css; grep -n \"breadcrumb\" src/components/onboarding/onboarding.css","description":"Extract onboarding and note-editor CSS to owners"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
