{"parentUuid":"9143e796-cfcf-43f9-a94f-64e947863fa9","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14658760 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"97b11797-6b25-412f-87ef-ffa45f665874","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:39:33.966Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14658760 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","hash":"0c31f94e90483852f59d6fe9e958f2f45e43ac7099449a22af9092672f98b6fc","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm leaning toward deleting ItemMedia.test.ts since it's just trivial formatting logic, but the alive.test.ts tests look like they guard against real regressions—things like eye spacing drift and splash bonus removal—so those seem worth keeping.\n\nI'm checking whether test 5's face-margin assertion overlaps with faceMargin.test.ts, since that would make it a duplicate worth deleting; if faceMargin.test.ts already covers eyes-inside-body for both sidebar and welcome mascots, test 5 is redundant. Test 4's eye-spacing check feels like a genuine unique regression guard worth keeping, even though it wasn't added by an explicit fix commit, since the keep criteria don't seem strictly limited to fix-commit tests.\n\nRevisiting the delete categories as the actual constraint rather than requiring everything to match the keep list, I'm going through each file more conservatively: for keyboardShortcuts, I'd drop the three key-mapping tests as mock-mirror/trivial but keep the \"doesn't steal keys from editors\" test since it reflects real user-facing behavior. For previewMode, I'd delete the hasPreviewQuery and env-flag tests as trivial but keep the two desktop-specific seedLibrary tests since they protect against seeds leaking into the real library. For SearchOutline, the first couple tests look like smoke/trivial checks I'd remove.\n\nFor the geometry test, I'd keep the \"corners stay near base radius\" regression guard and the \"gain 0 produces a straight rounded rect\" behavior check. For mascotStore, I'm setting a clearer rule: delete anything that's just a smoke assertion (no NaN, defined, length>N) or restates static data, but keep anything asserting a specific behavioral contract — so the \"notifies subscribers without rAF\" test stays since it guards real functionality, while I'm still weighing the notification/fallback tests case by case.\n\nOverall I'll keep mascotStore mostly intact, delete inklingSkins' static/smoke tests, trim alive tests 1–3 and any duplicate of faceMargin, drop the trivial ItemMedia formatting file, remove the duplicate assetUrlCache eviction test, and for imageZoom keep the anchor-under-cursor and fit/max-zoom-bound tests as real behavior contracts while leaning toward cutting the simple wheel-direction test since it's too trivial.\n\nFor noteMarkdown I'll delete the wheel-direction test as trivial, keep the persistence/round-trip markdown tests but drop the one duplicating note-markdown-01 and note-todo-01 coverage of headings/emphasis/links/tasks, while retaining the empty-content normalization test. I'll keep all liquidGlassShape tests explicitly, retain archiveGridWindow's windowing tests including the column-count fit test since it's part of the windowing behavior, and start reviewing readmeMascot's regression tests tied to several fix commits.\n\nAmong readmeMascot's 18 tests, I need to separate which came from the original feature commit versus later fix commits, and figure out whether tests like \"is a standalone document\" or \"parses as a document rather than just looking like markup\" belong under static-markup smoke checks — I'll open the 509-line file to decide. For faceMargin I'll keep it since it covers real eyes-inside-body behavior from the feature commit, and now I want to pull up both","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BKW8ZDrcuT3Em9cQtb7sDf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-a1f541e8 && sed -n 95,122p src/components/mascot/faceMargin.test.ts; sed -n 1,30p src/components/mascot/readmeMascot.test.ts; sed -n 120,250p src/components/mascot/readmeMascot.test.ts","description":"Read faceMargin and readmeMascot tests"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
