{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","hash":"1f0f7bb115de3e8b2eab3a204b5be34b7a38b3b1de6acc91ad9eeec29206bb48","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll keep all the persistence, migrations, queue, and ordering tests, plus the data directory precedence test since it's the Windows path-separator failure that's fine on Linux CI. Tallying up the deletions across ItemMedia, inklingSkins, alive, SearchOutline, previewMode, keyboard, assetUrl, imageZoom, and noteMarkdown files.\n\nTotaling these up: 39 in src plus 1 electron content-type test brings it to 40, so I need to delete that asset-response test too. I also want to check whether helper exports like formatDuration, formatFileSize, fileExtensionLabel, noteWordCount, hasPreviewQuery, isDevFlag, and isPreviewBuildFlag are still used elsewhere in the app, since knip will flag anything that becomes unused once their tests are removed.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm keeping storage.test.ts since it covers persistence, migrations, leases, and ordering. Next I'll trim the content-type fallback test from the electron tests, then run knip to catch any now-unused exports.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013BcALP4V98keEWZMUwU8sE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-a1f541e8 && python \"$TEMP/squ132/drop_tests.py\" electron/asset-response.test.ts \"unknown extensions fall back to a binary content type\" && unset ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE; bunx biome check --write --unsafe electron/asset-response.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -1; bun run knip 2>&1 | tail -15","description":"Drop asset content-type test, run knip","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
