{"parentUuid":"8bf49d15-29d6-47b5-96d1-1699f152cb3e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQYzAPgMqgKGx1di1peq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019hB7LeAebVpyrTMzCa2aSn","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8\\docs\\design.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":718,"cache_read_input_tokens":250191,"output_tokens":85,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":718,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":85,"cache_read_input_tokens":250191,"cache_creation_input_tokens":718,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":718},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019hB7LeAebVpyrTMzCa2aSn":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8\\docs\\design.md"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgQYzA3bBeXBfJxEhnkzK","requestRef":"26d43f1e-a9d2-4062-a90d-6a114c09e36a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4bfeede7-46f7-46ac-ae46-7ad20697a2b3","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:43:01.067Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
{"parentUuid":"4bfeede7-46f7-46ac-ae46-7ad20697a2b3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cda62929-1bba-4a09-ba3d-cc680eb61184","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019hB7LeAebVpyrTMzCa2aSn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# inkling visual direction\n2\t\n3\t## Direction\n4\t\n5\tA thoughtful canvas companion: a clean, modern workspace where the bloub mascot exists as a responsive companion, anchored but alive, enhancing the library experience through subtle, purposeful interactions while maintaining organized precision and Apple-esque animation craft. The interface balances mascot presence with UI cleanliness, never letting the companion dominate the workspace.\n6\t\n7\t## Composition\n8\t\n9\t- A left sidebar anchors navigation and Spaces with icon-based navigation.\n10\t- Search is the primary surface at the top with the mascot enveloping it on focus.\n11\t- Our mascot lives in the upper-right corner as a constant but unobtrusive presence.\n12\t- The library grid is the center of attention: notes, quotes, images, articles, documents, videos, etc. have disctint card treatments.\n13\t- The header is compact; the mascot provides personality without needing hero statements or dashboard metrics.\n14\t- The detail inspector appears only when an item is selected, with the mascot moving to the inspector's upper-right corner.\n15\t\n16\t## Materials and tokens\n17\t\n18\t- Canvas ground: `#faf9f6` (warm off-white)\n19\t- Ink primary: `#1a1a1a` (near-black for main content)\n20\t- Ink secondary: `#6b6b6b` (muted gray for supporting text)\n21\t- Rule/subtle: `#e8e6e1` (soft dividers and borders)\n22\t- Mascot body: `#1a1a1a` (same as ink primary for seamless integration)\n23\t- Mascot eyes: `#ffffff` (pure white for contrast)\n24\t- Mascot accent: `#ff7e5f` (soft coral for eye highlights/active states)\n25\t- Content-type accents: blue `#4a90e2`, orange `#f5a623`, green `#7ed321`, purple `#bd10e0`, red `#e74c3c`\n26\t- Card surface: `#ffffff` (pure white cards on canvas ground)\n27\t- Typography: System UI font stack (Inter/SF Pro/Segoe UI) at 15px body, 18px headlines, 13px secondary\n28\t- Radii: 14px for content surfaces (matching mascot's organic curves), 8px for controls\n29\t- Elevation: Single soft shadow `0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06)` on floating surfaces\n30\t\n31\t## mascot behavior\n32\t\n33\t- Home base: upper-right corner, in sidebar header paired with the app name \"inkling\"\n34\t- States: idle (flowy, wavy animation), observing (eyes follow cursor), processing (slightly faster waviness, eyes closed to look like a furrowed brow), delighted (bounce, eyes rotated upwards to look like smiling), sleeping (eyes close after inactivity, slowed down wavyness)\n35\t- (This is still being considered and may not be a part of the product) Content-type reactions: mascot morphs based on viewed content (reading posture for articles, wider eyes for images, thoughtful shape for notes, playful tilt for quotes)\n36\t- Contextual surfacing: leans toward search on focus, moves to center for empty states, celebrates successes, droops slightly on errors\n37\t- Movement: Physics-based drift within zone, 200-400ms transitions, never obscures content\n38\t- Accessibility: mascot never sole indicator of state, can be disabled in settings, respects motion preferences\n39\t\n40\t## Interaction grammar\n41\t\n42\t- Search is the primary action and remains visible, with mascot enhancing the experience through contextual reactions.\n43\t- Motion follows Apple-like principles: purposeful (communicates something), subtle (never draws attention), consistent (similar timing), performant (60fps).\n44\t- Timing standards: 150ms for micro-interactions, 200-300ms for mascot morphs, 300ms for layout transitions, 400ms for delight moments.\n45\t- Easing: Default `cubic-bezier(0.4, 0.0, 0.2, 1)`, mascot movement `cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1)` for organic feel.\n46\t"}]},"uuid":"5b018452-770b-4052-a6db-da2b4f0d2d70","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:43:01.213Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8\\docs\\design.md","content":"# inkling visual direction\n\n## Direction\n\nA thoughtful canvas companion: a clean, modern workspace where the bloub mascot exists as a responsive companion, anchored but alive, enhancing the library experience through subtle, purposeful interactions while maintaining organized precision and Apple-esque animation craft. The interface balances mascot presence with UI cleanliness, never letting the companion dominate the workspace.\n\n## Composition\n\n- A left sidebar anchors navigation and Spaces with icon-based navigation.\n- Search is the primary surface at the top with the mascot enveloping it on focus.\n- Our mascot lives in the upper-right corner as a constant but unobtrusive presence.\n- The library grid is the center of attention: notes, quotes, images, articles, documents, videos, etc. have disctint card treatments.\n- The header is compact; the mascot provides personality without needing hero statements or dashboard metrics.\n- The detail inspector appears only when an item is selected, with the mascot moving to the inspector's upper-right corner.\n\n## Materials and tokens\n\n- Canvas ground: `#faf9f6` (warm off-white)\n- Ink primary: `#1a1a1a` (near-black for main content)\n- Ink secondary: `#6b6b6b` (muted gray for supporting text)\n- Rule/subtle: `#e8e6e1` (soft dividers and borders)\n- Mascot body: `#1a1a1a` (same as ink primary for seamless integration)\n- Mascot eyes: `#ffffff` (pure white for contrast)\n- Mascot accent: `#ff7e5f` (soft coral for eye highlights/active states)\n- Content-type accents: blue `#4a90e2`, orange `#f5a623`, green `#7ed321`, purple `#bd10e0`, red `#e74c3c`\n- Card surface: `#ffffff` (pure white cards on canvas ground)\n- Typography: System UI font stack (Inter/SF Pro/Segoe UI) at 15px body, 18px headlines, 13px secondary\n- Radii: 14px for content surfaces (matching mascot's organic curves), 8px for controls\n- Elevation: Single soft shadow `0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06)` on floating surfaces\n\n## mascot behavior\n\n- Home base: upper-right corner, in sidebar header paired with the app name \"inkling\"\n- States: idle (flowy, wavy animation), observing (eyes follow cursor), processing (slightly faster waviness, eyes closed to look like a furrowed brow), delighted (bounce, eyes rotated upwards to look like smiling), sleeping (eyes close after inactivity, slowed down wavyness)\n- (This is still being considered and may not be a part of the product) Content-type reactions: mascot morphs based on viewed content (reading posture for articles, wider eyes for images, thoughtful shape for notes, playful tilt for quotes)\n- Contextual surfacing: leans toward search on focus, moves to center for empty states, celebrates successes, droops slightly on errors\n- Movement: Physics-based drift within zone, 200-400ms transitions, never obscures content\n- Accessibility: mascot never sole indicator of state, can be disabled in settings, respects motion preferences\n\n## Interaction grammar\n\n- Search is the primary action and remains visible, with mascot enhancing the experience through contextual reactions.\n- Motion follows Apple-like principles: purposeful (communicates something), subtle (never draws attention), consistent (similar timing), performant (60fps).\n- Timing standards: 150ms for micro-interactions, 200-300ms for mascot morphs, 300ms for layout transitions, 400ms for delight moments.\n- Easing: Default `cubic-bezier(0.4, 0.0, 0.2, 1)`, mascot movement `cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1)` for organic feel.\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4bfeede7-46f7-46ac-ae46-7ad20697a2b3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
