{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","hash":"061146707d8e2711557e95e860ad27ab27a13c9045b81151c1cb229ee9439580","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I shouldI should update the \"Materials and tokens\" section to reference the real dark tokens from index.css's @theme rather than enumerating fields, pointing to src/index.css as the source of truth while listing the core palette. I also want to fix the composition line about item view to reflect that an open item now replaces the library frame with media on a dotted stage and an inspector on the right, leaving mascot placement untouched since that's product intent, and add a note about liquid glass materials on floating controls.\n\nI'm drafting the token list now, covering ground colors, surfaces, borders, ink tones, and accent colors with their hex values, plus typography fonts and radii values for buttons, cards, and overlays.\n\nCard radii go up to 20px for cards and search, 24px for overlays. Glass effects apply to floating controls above the library like the view dock, zoom pill, and menus, with liquid refraction via WebGPU in the desktop app and a CSS blur fallback elsewhere, but grid cards should never have glass — so I need to check whether that duration badge on LibraryCard is violating that rule.\n\nI'm wondering if this glass badge predates my changes, since LibraryCard was extracted from App.tsx in SQU-129","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Before documenting glass as \"never on grid cards\", I'll check whether the glass badge in LibraryCard predates this stack."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LeFbBpRAXwTgfvZotyuZBf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-a1f541e8 && sed -n 150,165p src/features/library/LibraryCard.tsx; git show main:src/App.tsx | grep -n 'glass' | head -10","description":"Check card glass badge origin on main"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
