{"parentUuid":"9014faf1-5cdc-4cda-ac0c-8373c0806235","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQZ1bkCjbnu2w9J5SEYY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Main already has the glass video pill on cards, so that's parity. Writing the docs now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2173,"cache_read_input_tokens":252437,"output_tokens":1865,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":174},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2173,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1865,"cache_read_input_tokens":252437,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2173,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2173},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgQZ1bNsmcPPUCHU1LCuK","requestRef":"e9d8742e-a5d5-4aae-9c85-0eb06a2693e7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c4b266e1-de15-444b-ac16-a532985d9db4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:43:24.408Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
{"parentUuid":"c4b266e1-de15-444b-ac16-a532985d9db4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQZ1bkCjbnu2w9J5SEYY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XgV2F11HNSpB5yjPVUM4EK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python - <<'EOF'\np='docs/tech-stack.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold='''| Styling | Tailwind CSS plus accessible headless primitives | Fast iteration without locking the product to a heavy component theme |\n| Client state | Zustand | Small, explicit state layer for UI state |\n| Server-style data state | TanStack Query | Caching and invalidation for asynchronous repository calls |\n'''\nnew='''| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 utilities, Base UI headless primitives, and a WebGPU liquid glass layer | Fast iteration without locking the product to a heavy component theme |\n| UI state | React hooks per feature, composed in `App` | The renderer's state is small and local; library rows are patched by item id instead of cached and invalidated |\n'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nanchor='## Article extraction'\nsection='''## Styling\n\nComponents style themselves with Tailwind utilities against the tokens in `src/index.css`. Base UI supplies behavior and accessibility for dialogs, tabs, menus and buttons, with no theme of its own. Plain CSS files are kept only where utilities can't reach: `reader.css` and the note editor style HTML they don't render themselves, onboarding runs on keyframes, and Sonner's toasts are styled through its data attributes. Those files sit next to the component that owns them.\n\nFloating controls over the library are glass. In the desktop app, `LiquidGlass` renders the library inside a `<canvas layoutsubtree>`, Chromium's HTML-in-Canvas copies it into a WebGPU texture, and refracting glass is drawn under every `.glass` element. `.glass` and `.css-glass` both start as a blurred CSS glass. `LiquidGlass` marks a `.glass` element with `data-liquid` once its canvas draws it, which clears the CSS glass. `.css-glass` is for surfaces outside a canvas, and always stays CSS. The web preview, machines without WebGPU, and a lost GPU device keep the CSS glass. Each liquid surface costs GPU time, so glass stays on a few floating controls and never on card surfaces.\n\n'''\nassert anchor in s; s=s.replace(anchor, section+anchor,1)\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='\\n').write(s)\n\np='docs/design.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\na=s.index('## Materials and tokens')\nb=s.index('## mascot behavior')\nnew='''## Materials and tokens\n\nTokens live in the `@theme` block of `src/index.css`. Use their Tailwind names (`bg-surface`, `text-muted`, `rounded-card`) rather than raw values.\n\n- Ground: dark and warm. App `#0a0a09`, canvas `#0c0c0b`, library frame `#0d0c0b`.\n- Surfaces: `#161412`, raised `#1b1917`, borders `#262221`.\n- Ink: `#e5ddd2`, soft `#c9c1b6`, muted `#8d867c`.\n- Accent: copper `#b0714f` (soft `#241c16`) for focus rings, selection and the primary action. Green `#7fa08d` marks processing that is going well.\n- Paper tints for notes and quotes: blue `#243136`, green `#26332c`, yellow `#3a3524`.\n- Space colors: orange (the accent), green `#7f9a8c`, blue `#8e9bbf`, pink `#c98b8b`, purple `#a88ab5`, yellow `#c9b27a`.\n- Type: the system UI stack for body text, DM Sans for display, DM Mono for sizes and counts, Libre Baskerville for quotes and note headings.\n- Radii: 9px buttons and rows, 12px toggles and tiles, 14px sidebar, 16px library frame, 20px cards and search, 24px overlays.\n- Glass: floating controls over the library are glass. In the desktop app it is liquid glass refracting the library through WebGPU. The web preview and machines without WebGPU get a blurred CSS glass. Card surfaces never get glass.\n\n'''\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"- The detail inspector appears only when an item is selected, with the mascot moving to the inspector's upper-right corner.\",\n\"- An open item replaces the library frame: its media sits on a dotted stage, with an inspector on the right.\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='\\n').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat docs","description":"Rewrite tech-stack styling and design tokens"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2173,"cache_read_input_tokens":252437,"output_tokens":1865,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":174},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2173,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1865,"cache_read_input_tokens":252437,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2173,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2173},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XgV2F11HNSpB5yjPVUM4EK":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-a1f541e8 && python - <<'EOF'\np='docs/tech-stack.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold='''| Styling | Tailwind CSS plus accessible headless primitives | Fast iteration without locking the product to a heavy component theme |\n| Client state | Zustand | Small, explicit state layer for UI state |\n| Server-style data state | TanStack Query | Caching and invalidation for asynchronous repository calls |\n'''\nnew='''| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 utilities, Base UI headless primitives, and a WebGPU liquid glass layer | Fast iteration without locking the product to a heavy component theme |\n| UI state | React hooks per feature, composed in `App` | The renderer's state is small and local; library rows are patched by item id instead of cached and invalidated |\n'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nanchor='## Article extraction'\nsection='''## Styling\n\nComponents style themselves with Tailwind utilities against the tokens in `src/index.css`. Base UI supplies behavior and accessibility for dialogs, tabs, menus and buttons, with no theme of its own. Plain CSS files are kept only where utilities can't reach: `reader.css` and the note editor style HTML they don't render themselves, onboarding runs on keyframes, and Sonner's toasts are styled through its data attributes. Those files sit next to the component that owns them.\n\nFloating controls over the library are glass. In the desktop app, `LiquidGlass` renders the library inside a `<canvas layoutsubtree>`, Chromium's HTML-in-Canvas copies it into a WebGPU texture, and refracting glass is drawn under every `.glass` element. `.glass` and `.css-glass` both start as a blurred CSS glass. `LiquidGlass` marks a `.glass` element with `data-liquid` once its canvas draws it, which clears the CSS glass. `.css-glass` is for surfaces outside a canvas, and always stays CSS. The web preview, machines without WebGPU, and a lost GPU device keep the CSS glass. Each liquid surface costs GPU time, so glass stays on a few floating controls and never on card surfaces.\n\n'''\nassert anchor in s; s=s.replace(anchor, section+anchor,1)\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='\\n').write(s)\n\np='docs/design.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\na=s.index('## Materials and tokens')\nb=s.index('## mascot behavior')\nnew='''## Materials and tokens\n\nTokens live in the `@theme` block of `src/index.css`. Use their Tailwind names (`bg-surface`, `text-muted`, `rounded-card`) rather than raw values.\n\n- Ground: dark and warm. App `#0a0a09`, canvas `#0c0c0b`, library frame `#0d0c0b`.\n- Surfaces: `#161412`, raised `#1b1917`, borders `#262221`.\n- Ink: `#e5ddd2`, soft `#c9c1b6`, muted `#8d867c`.\n- Accent: copper `#b0714f` (soft `#241c16`) for focus rings, selection and the primary action. Green `#7fa08d` marks processing that is going well.\n- Paper tints for notes and quotes: blue `#243136`, green `#26332c`, yellow `#3a3524`.\n- Space colors: orange (the accent), green `#7f9a8c`, blue `#8e9bbf`, pink `#c98b8b`, purple `#a88ab5`, yellow `#c9b27a`.\n- Type: the system UI stack for body text, DM Sans for display, DM Mono for sizes and counts, Libre Baskerville for quotes and note headings.\n- Radii: 9px buttons and rows, 12px toggles and tiles, 14px sidebar, 16px library frame, 20px cards and search, 24px overlays.\n- Glass: floating controls over the library are glass. In the desktop app it is liquid glass refracting the library through WebGPU. The web preview and machines without WebGPU get a blurred CSS glass. Card surfaces never get glass.\n\n'''\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"- The detail inspector appears only when an item is selected, with the mascot moving to the inspector's upper-right corner.\",\n\"- An open item replaces the library frame: its media sits on a dotted stage, with an inspector on the right.\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='\\n').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat docs","description":"Rewrite tech-stack styling and design tokens"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01XgV2F11HNSpB5yjPVUM4EK":{"cwd":"/c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-a1f541e8"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgQZ1bNsmcPPUCHU1LCuK","requestRef":"e9d8742e-a5d5-4aae-9c85-0eb06a2693e7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c8a9f28f-b02e-4336-ade8-e3268807084e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:43:34.762Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
{"parentUuid":"c8a9f28f-b02e-4336-ade8-e3268807084e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cda62929-1bba-4a09-ba3d-cc680eb61184","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XgV2F11HNSpB5yjPVUM4EK","type":"tool_result","content":"warning: in the working copy of 'docs/design.md', LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it\nwarning: in the working copy of 'docs/tech-stack.md', LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it\n docs/design.md     | 25 ++++++++++++-------------\n docs/tech-stack.md | 11 ++++++++---\n 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0d21a671-5e9b-47af-81db-0581362f2531","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:43:36.134Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"warning: in the working copy of 'docs/design.md', LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it\nwarning: in the working copy of 'docs/tech-stack.md', LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it\n docs/design.md     | 25 ++++++++++++-------------\n docs/tech-stack.md | 11 ++++++++---\n 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8\\docs\\design.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":22,"newStart":11,"newLines":21,"lines":[" - Our mascot lives in the upper-right corner as a constant but unobtrusive presence."," - The library grid is the center of attention: notes, quotes, images, articles, documents, videos, etc. have disctint card treatments."," - The header is compact; the mascot provides personality without needing hero statements or dashboard metrics.","-- The detail inspector appears only when an item is selected, with the mascot moving to the inspector's upper-right corner.","+- An open item replaces the library frame: its media sits on a dotted stage, with an inspector on the right."," "," ## Materials and tokens"," ","-- Canvas ground: `#faf9f6` (warm off-white)","-- Ink primary: `#1a1a1a` (near-black for main content)","-- Ink secondary: `#6b6b6b` (muted gray for supporting text)","-- Rule/subtle: `#e8e6e1` (soft dividers and borders)","-- Mascot body: `#1a1a1a` (same as ink primary for seamless integration)","-- Mascot eyes: `#ffffff` (pure white for contrast)","-- Mascot accent: `#ff7e5f` (soft coral for eye highlights/active states)","-- Content-type accents: blue `#4a90e2`, orange `#f5a623`, green `#7ed321`, purple `#bd10e0`, red `#e74c3c`","-- Card surface: `#ffffff` (pure white cards on canvas ground)","-- Typography: System UI font stack (Inter/SF Pro/Segoe UI) at 15px body, 18px headlines, 13px secondary","-- Radii: 14px for content surfaces (matching mascot's organic curves), 8px for controls","-- Elevation: Single soft shadow `0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06)` on floating surfaces","+Tokens live in the `@theme` block of `src/index.css`. Use their Tailwind names (`bg-surface`, `text-muted`, `rounded-card`) rather than raw values.","+","+- Ground: dark and warm. App `#0a0a09`, canvas `#0c0c0b`, library frame `#0d0c0b`.","+- Surfaces: `#161412`, raised `#1b1917`, borders `#262221`.","+- Ink: `#e5ddd2`, soft `#c9c1b6`, muted `#8d867c`.","+- Accent: copper `#b0714f` (soft `#241c16`) for focus rings, selection and the primary action. Green `#7fa08d` marks processing that is going well.","+- Paper tints for notes and quotes: blue `#243136`, green `#26332c`, yellow `#3a3524`.","+- Space colors: orange (the accent), green `#7f9a8c`, blue `#8e9bbf`, pink `#c98b8b`, purple `#a88ab5`, yellow `#c9b27a`.","+- Type: the system UI stack for body text, DM Sans for display, DM Mono for sizes and counts, Libre Baskerville for quotes and note headings.","+- Radii: 9px buttons and rows, 12px toggles and tiles, 14px sidebar, 16px library frame, 20px cards and search, 24px overlays.","+- Glass: floating controls over the library are glass. In the desktop app it is liquid glass refracting the library through WebGPU. The web preview and machines without WebGPU get a blurred CSS glass. Card surfaces never get glass."," "," ## mascot behavior"," "]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8\\docs\\tech-stack.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":15,"newStart":14,"newLines":20,"lines":[" |---|---|---|"," | Desktop shell | Electron 44 | Windows desktop packaging with a reusable web frontend and a narrow preload bridge |"," | UI | React + TypeScript + Vite | Mature component ecosystem and future web portability |","-| Styling | Tailwind CSS plus accessible headless primitives | Fast iteration without locking the product to a heavy component theme |","-| Client state | Zustand | Small, explicit state layer for UI state |","-| Server-style data state | TanStack Query | Caching and invalidation for asynchronous repository calls |","+| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 utilities, Base UI headless primitives, and a WebGPU liquid glass layer | Fast iteration without locking the product to a heavy component theme |","+| UI state | React hooks per feature, composed in `App` | The renderer's state is small and local; library rows are patched by item id instead of cached and invalidated |"," | Application core | Electron main process and Node.js | File, job queue, database, and model-process orchestration |"," | Database | SQLite through `node:sqlite` | Direct control over migrations, transactions, and FTS5 |"," | Exact search | SQLite FTS5 | Local full-text search across content, notes, OCR, and summaries |"," | Asset storage | Content-addressed local files | Avoid duplicate assets and make backup/restore predictable |"," | Background work | Node.js job queue persisted in SQLite | Retryable processing without blocking the UI |"," ","+## Styling","+","+Components style themselves with Tailwind utilities against the tokens in `src/index.css`. Base UI supplies behavior and accessibility for dialogs, tabs, menus and buttons, with no theme of its own. Plain CSS files are kept only where utilities can't reach: `reader.css` and the note editor style HTML they don't render themselves, onboarding runs on keyframes, and Sonner's toasts are styled through its data attributes. Those files sit next to the component that owns them.","+","+Floating controls over the library are glass. In the desktop app, `LiquidGlass` renders the library inside a `<canvas layoutsubtree>`, Chromium's HTML-in-Canvas copies it into a WebGPU texture, and refracting glass is drawn under every `.glass` element. `.glass` and `.css-glass` both start as a blurred CSS glass. `LiquidGlass` marks a `.glass` element with `data-liquid` once its canvas draws it, which clears the CSS glass. `.css-glass` is for surfaces outside a canvas, and always stays CSS. The web preview, machines without WebGPU, and a lost GPU device keep the CSS glass. Each liquid surface costs GPU time, so glass stays on a few floating controls and never on card surfaces.","+"," ## Article extraction"," "," Use Defuddle as the initial article extraction engine rather than implementing a new readability parser or forking Defuddle."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8\\docs\\design.md","C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8\\docs\\tech-stack.md"]}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c8a9f28f-b02e-4336-ade8-e3268807084e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
{"parentUuid":"0d21a671-5e9b-47af-81db-0581362f2531","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14616699 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e36a9d14-60ce-4db0-ac95-b5ededc967b3","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:43:36.154Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14616699 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","hash":"79b334b8886747ca74307d91dfd2fc6f8db48a2f5031761b2625f253779b921c","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm confirming the video pill on cards is the only glass element on card surfaces, since glass stays reserved for floating controls rather than card backgrounds. Now I'm moving on to writing the tech-stack docs.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Main already has the glass video pill on cards, so that's parity. Writing the docs now."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XgV2F11HNSpB5yjPVUM4EK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-a1f541e8 && python - <<'EOF'\np='docs/tech-stack.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold='''| Styling | Tailwind CSS plus accessible headless primitives | Fast iteration without locking the product to a heavy component theme |\n| Client state | Zustand | Small, explicit state layer for UI state |\n| Server-style data state | TanStack Query | Caching and invalidation for asynchronous repository calls |\n'''\nnew='''| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 utilities, Base UI headless primitives, and a WebGPU liquid glass layer | Fast iteration without locking the product to a heavy component theme |\n| UI state | React hooks per feature, composed in `App` | The renderer's state is small and local; library rows are patched by item id instead of cached and invalidated |\n'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nanchor='## Article extraction'\nsection='''## Styling\n\nComponents style themselves with Tailwind utilities against the tokens in `src/index.css`. Base UI supplies behavior and accessibility for dialogs, tabs, menus and buttons, with no theme of its own. Plain CSS files are kept only where utilities can't reach: `reader.css` and the note editor style HTML they don't render themselves, onboarding runs on keyframes, and Sonner's toasts are styled through its data attributes. Those files sit next to the component that owns them.\n\nFloating controls over the library are glass. In the desktop app, `LiquidGlass` renders the library inside a `<canvas layoutsubtree>`, Chromium's HTML-in-Canvas copies it into a WebGPU texture, and refracting glass is drawn under every `.glass` element. `.glass` and `.css-glass` both start as a blurred CSS glass. `LiquidGlass` marks a `.glass` element with `data-liquid` once its canvas draws it, which clears the CSS glass. `.css-glass` is for surfaces outside a canvas, and always stays CSS. The web preview, machines without WebGPU, and a lost GPU device keep the CSS glass. Each liquid surface costs GPU time, so glass stays on a few floating controls and never on card surfaces.\n\n'''\nassert anchor in s; s=s.replace(anchor, section+anchor,1)\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='\\n').write(s)\n\np='docs/design.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\na=s.index('## Materials and tokens')\nb=s.index('## mascot behavior')\nnew='''## Materials and tokens\n\nTokens live in the `@theme` block of `src/index.css`. Use their Tailwind names (`bg-surface`, `text-muted`, `rounded-card`) rather than raw values.\n\n- Ground: dark and warm. App `#0a0a09`, canvas `#0c0c0b`, library frame `#0d0c0b`.\n- Surfaces: `#161412`, raised `#1b1917`, borders `#262221`.\n- Ink: `#e5ddd2`, soft `#c9c1b6`, muted `#8d867c`.\n- Accent: copper `#b0714f` (soft `#241c16`) for focus rings, selection and the primary action. Green `#7fa08d` marks processing that is going well.\n- Paper tints for notes and quotes: blue `#243136`, green `#26332c`, yellow `#3a3524`.\n- Space colors: orange (the accent), green `#7f9a8c`, blue `#8e9bbf`, pink `#c98b8b`, purple `#a88ab5`, yellow `#c9b27a`.\n- Type: the system UI stack for body text, DM Sans for display, DM Mono for sizes and counts, Libre Baskerville for quotes and note headings.\n- Radii: 9px buttons and rows, 12px toggles and tiles, 14px sidebar, 16px library frame, 20px cards and search, 24px overlays.\n- Glass: floating controls over the library are glass. In the desktop app it is liquid glass refracting the library through WebGPU. The web preview and machines without WebGPU get a blurred CSS glass. Card surfaces never get glass.\n\n'''\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"- The detail inspector appears only when an item is selected, with the mascot moving to the inspector's upper-right corner.\",\n\"- An open item replaces the library frame: its media sits on a dotted stage, with an inspector on the right.\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='\\n').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat docs","description":"Rewrite tech-stack styling and design tokens"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
