{"parentUuid":"65c38918-bd7f-4557-bbc0-9e3015a30d28","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cda62929-1bba-4a09-ba3d-cc680eb61184","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013b6rramjWroYZ2FbpZ22EF","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/models.md:14:artifacts pinned to known Hugging Face revisions and verifies their SHA-256\ndocs/models.md:22:The Windows installer bundles the pinned model files in the Electron resources\ndocs/tech-stack.md:99:Nomic Embed Text v1.5 and Nomic Embed Vision v1.5 are the initial learned embedding pair. They are downloaded as pinned INT8 ONNX artifacts into the app model cache on the first indexing run, with SHA-256 verification before use. Models will still be evaluated using a representative local test corpus, not by reputation alone. Revisit the choice if semantic search relevance, image similarity relevance, CPU time, RAM usage, GPU acceleration, download size, cold-start time, or batch processing time is not acceptable.\ndocs/operations/development.md:7:1. Install Bun 1.4.2 (pinned in `.bun-version` and `package.json#packageManager`).\ndocs/operations/development.md:33:The Electron release package includes the pinned embedding models under its\ndocs/operations/development.md:47:| Everything | `bun run check` | Bun pin, frozen install (`--ignore-scripts`), typecheck of every workspace, tests, Knip, lint, both builds, ingestion smoke, extension build. CI runs the same steps as separate jobs |\ndocs/operations/development.md:52:| Bun pin | `bun run check:bun-version` | `.bun-version` vs `packageManager` vs running Bun must agree |\ndocs/operations/development.md:63:- `ci.yml`: docs-only pushes skip; otherwise the frontend job verifies the Bun version pin, typechecks every workspace, runs tests, `knip`, builds the app and extension, and runs ingestion smoke tests.\ndocs/operations/development.md:67:- `electron-preview.yml`: when a same-repository PR has the `preview:win` label, builds and uploads the Windows Electron installer. Electron changes also build the Linux directory package and launch it under Xvfb; pinned model files are cached only in GitHub Actions.\ndocs/operations/development.md:72:- `Expected Bun X, found Y`: install the pinned Bun from `.bun-version`; don't edit the check to match your install.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"77b9e718-91ce-43d3-9cf9-528465fb013e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:44:19.510Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"docs/models.md:14:artifacts pinned to known Hugging Face revisions and verifies their SHA-256\ndocs/models.md:22:The Windows installer bundles the pinned model files in the Electron resources\ndocs/tech-stack.md:99:Nomic Embed Text v1.5 and Nomic Embed Vision v1.5 are the initial learned embedding pair. They are downloaded as pinned INT8 ONNX artifacts into the app model cache on the first indexing run, with SHA-256 verification before use. Models will still be evaluated using a representative local test corpus, not by reputation alone. Revisit the choice if semantic search relevance, image similarity relevance, CPU time, RAM usage, GPU acceleration, download size, cold-start time, or batch processing time is not acceptable.\ndocs/operations/development.md:7:1. Install Bun 1.4.2 (pinned in `.bun-version` and `package.json#packageManager`).\ndocs/operations/development.md:33:The Electron release package includes the pinned embedding models under its\ndocs/operations/development.md:47:| Everything | `bun run check` | Bun pin, frozen install (`--ignore-scripts`), typecheck of every workspace, tests, Knip, lint, both builds, ingestion smoke, extension build. CI runs the same steps as separate jobs |\ndocs/operations/development.md:52:| Bun pin | `bun run check:bun-version` | `.bun-version` vs `packageManager` vs running Bun must agree |\ndocs/operations/development.md:63:- `ci.yml`: docs-only pushes skip; otherwise the frontend job verifies the Bun version pin, typechecks every workspace, runs tests, `knip`, builds the app and extension, and runs ingestion smoke tests.\ndocs/operations/development.md:67:- `electron-preview.yml`: when a same-repository PR has the `preview:win` label, builds and uploads the Windows Electron installer. Electron changes also build the Linux directory package and launch it under Xvfb; pinned model files are cached only in GitHub Actions.\ndocs/operations/development.md:72:- `Expected Bun X, found Y`: install the pinned Bun from `.bun-version`; don't edit the check to match your install.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"65c38918-bd7f-4557-bbc0-9e3015a30d28","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
