ernal","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
{"parentUuid":"0a992adc-2587-4133-be15-f7fac02d99eb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cda62929-1bba-4a09-ba3d-cc680eb61184","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GHeeKDucGpQueqK5Ltu8WT","type":"tool_result","content":"# Changelog\n\nAll notable development phases and changes are recorded here. See also [roadmap.md](roadmap.md) for what comes next.\n\nThe best times to update this file so as to minimize friction while working with a developer or contributor are:\n1. When completing a medium-large implementation pass of features, bug fixes, performance enhancements, refactoring updates, or likewise changes\n2. The user indicates, whether directly or indirectly through their actions, they want to or are going to finish up the local work and merge the changes afterwards\n3. Before starting a new, unrelated task — close out the entry for the work just finished rather than letting it blur or get jumbled into the next thing\n4. When a change alters public behavior: API contracts, CLI flags, config options, env vars; anything a user of the project depends on being stable\n\nChangelog entry format: \n\n- Follow [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/): group entries under `Added`, `Changed`, `Fixed`, `Removed`, `Deprecated`, `Security`.\n- Each entry is one line, written for a human reader — what changed in simple technical terms that someone could understand with simple google searches, not a commit message or file diff summary.\n- Reference issue/PR numbers or ticket IDs when they exist\n- Keep an `Unreleased` section at the top; move entries under a version heading at release time\n\nGuardrails:\n- Never mention that changes were made by an AI agent or even a developer — write entries as if the changes were just made\n- Don't editorialize or pad entries to look more substantial than the change was\n- If a change is trivial (typo fix, formatting, comment-only), skip the changelog — not every commit needs an entry\n- Ask before rewriting or reordering existing changelog history when you notice it is drifting from the required structure; only append.\n- When restructuring this document NO important/crucial/technical details should be lost\n\n\n\n## Unreleased\n\n### Added\n\n- Right-click a card to read, open its link, copy its link, show it in its folder, or archive it, from a menu in the library's glass (#170)\n- Buttons show a short label on hover or keyboard focus, in the same glass as the controls around them (#170)\n- Settings → General → Open source licenses lists every shipped dependency, vendored component, and bundled model with its license text and source, searchable and filterable by license (#170)\n- Settings → Appearance switches components between alternative looks while we compare them, the grid/list toggle as the current pill or a coss ui segmented control, and the sidebar button as buttons in the sidebar header and toolbar or a grip on the library frame's edge (#170)\n- Ctrl+\\ (⌘+\\ on a Mac) shows or hides the sidebar (#170)\n- First-run welcome flow on first launch of the installed app, replayable from Settings → General\n- PDF cards now show page-one thumbnails generated in the background after capture; existing PDFs are backfilled one at a time when the job queue is idle.\n- Chrome MV3 extension saves a page or right-clicked link through inkling's local capture receiver, with the existing capture link as fallback.\n- `bun run ui:smoke` drives the core library flows in Electron against a scratch profile and fails on console errors\n- Electron desktop shell alongside Tauri, with scoped `app://` assets, an IPC command allowlist, and `inkling://` capture links.\n27:## Unreleased\n29:### Added\n74:### Fixed\n94:### Changed\n132:### Removed\n139:### Fixed\n176:## Phase 5 -- Reading and Writing (Aug 25, 2026)\n178:### Added\n186:## Phase 4 -- PDF, Embeddings, CI (Aug 17-18, 2026)\n190:### Added\n201:### Fixed\n210:## Phase 3 -- Background OCR (Aug 15, 2026)\n214:### Added\n220:### Fixed\n227:## Phase 2 -- Benchmarks and Extraction Quality (Aug 14, 2026)\n231:### Added\n237:### Fixed\n246:### Added\n256:## Phase 1 -- Bootstrap (Aug 13-14, 2026)\n258:### Added","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b15a8f18-43f8-4542-a01c-ebfefca3f6ef","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:44:23.146Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Changelog\n\nAll notable development phases and changes are recorded here. See also [roadmap.md](roadmap.md) for what comes next.\n\nThe best times to update this file so as to minimize friction while working with a developer or contributor are:\n1. When completing a medium-large implementation pass of features, bug fixes, performance enhancements, refactoring updates, or likewise changes\n2. The user indicates, whether directly or indirectly through their actions, they want to or are going to finish up the local work and merge the changes afterwards\n3. Before starting a new, unrelated task — close out the entry for the work just finished rather than letting it blur or get jumbled into the next thing\n4. When a change alters public behavior: API contracts, CLI flags, config options, env vars; anything a user of the project depends on being stable\n\nChangelog entry format: \n\n- Follow [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/): group entries under `Added`, `Changed`, `Fixed`, `Removed`, `Deprecated`, `Security`.\n- Each entry is one line, written for a human reader — what changed in simple technical terms that someone could understand with simple google searches, not a commit message or file diff summary.\n- Reference issue/PR numbers or ticket IDs when they exist\n- Keep an `Unreleased` section at the top; move entries under a version heading at release time\n\nGuardrails:\n- Never mention that changes were made by an AI agent or even a developer — write entries as if the changes were just made\n- Don't editorialize or pad entries to look more substantial than the change was\n- If a change is trivial (typo fix, formatting, comment-only), skip the changelog — not every commit needs an entry\n- Ask before rewriting or reordering existing changelog history when you notice it is drifting from the required structure; only append.\n- When restructuring this document NO important/crucial/technical details should be lost\n\n\n\n## Unreleased\n\n### Added\n\n- Right-click a card to read, open its link, copy its link, show it in its folder, or archive it, from a menu in the library's glass (#170)\n- Buttons show a short label on hover or keyboard focus, in the same glass as the controls around them (#170)\n- Settings → General → Open source licenses lists every shipped dependency, vendored component, and bundled model with its license text and source, searchable and filterable by license (#170)\n- Settings → Appearance switches components between alternative looks while we compare them, the grid/list toggle as the current pill or a coss ui segmented control, and the sidebar button as buttons in the sidebar header and toolbar or a grip on the library frame's edge (#170)\n- Ctrl+\\ (⌘+\\ on a Mac) shows or hides the sidebar (#170)\n- First-run welcome flow on first launch of the installed app, replayable from Settings → General\n- PDF cards now show page-one thumbnails generated in the background after capture; existing PDFs are backfilled one at a time when the job queue is idle.\n- Chrome MV3 extension saves a page or right-clicked link through inkling's local capture receiver, with the existing capture link as fallback.\n- `bun run ui:smoke` drives the core library flows in Electron against a scratch profile and fails on console errors\n- Electron desktop shell alongside Tauri, with scoped `app://` assets, an IPC command allowlist, and `inkling://` capture links.\n27:## Unreleased\n29:### Added\n74:### Fixed\n94:### Changed\n132:### Removed\n139:### Fixed\n176:## Phase 5 -- Reading and Writing (Aug 25, 2026)\n178:### Added\n186:## Phase 4 -- PDF, Embeddings, CI (Aug 17-18, 2026)\n190:### Added\n201:### Fixed\n210:## Phase 3 -- Background OCR (Aug 15, 2026)\n214:### Added\n220:### Fixed\n227:## Phase 2 -- Benchmarks and Extraction Quality (Aug 14, 2026)\n231:### Added\n237:### Fixed\n246:### Added\n256:## Phase 1 -- Bootstrap (Aug 13-14, 2026)\n258:### Added","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0a992adc-2587-4133-be15-f7fac02d99eb","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
