{"parentUuid":"9953d8fe-c880-4578-b968-3cd2831b6e93","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cda62929-1bba-4a09-ba3d-cc680eb61184","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, Grep, PowerShell, Read, Skill, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write, mcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_issue, mcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_comments, mcp__claude_ai_Linear__save_comment, mcp__claude_ai_Linear__save_issue, mcp__t3-code__link_pull_request, mcp__t3-code__preview_evaluate, mcp__t3-code__preview_open, mcp__t3-code__preview_resize, mcp__t3-code__preview_snapshot</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent**\n\n   **Original `/goal`** (standing directive; don't pause to ask):\n   > \"Own the inkling UI refactor end to end: SQU-124 (tracker) and SQU-125 to SQU-132. Work until all are done; don't pause between layers. Read AGENTS.md (binding). Before starting any issue, read its description and every comment on it. The comments are newer and win wherever they differ from the description. SQU-124's \"Brief\" comment holds the rules for every layer (gate, mechanics, comments, tests, verify, stop, done); re-read it at each layer. Gate: #131 and #171 merged into main, and a clean worktree. Otherwise report and stop. Order: SQU-125 branches off main, any time. Then 126 → 132, each branched from and PR'd against the previous; 126 targets main. You have standing approval to open these PRs as drafts; mark each ready once it's verified and `bun run check` is green. Never: change visible behavior without sign-off, fork the glass Surface, put glass or Base UI in grid cards, regress #174's data path or App()'s ordering guarantees, or wait on sleeps. Report briefly at each PR. Finish with a summary comment on SQU-124.\"\n\n   #131 and #171 were closed without merging, so we proceed as if the gate is lifted.\n\n   **SQU-124 Brief** (re-read this layer)\n   - Parity port only. A visible behavior change needs sign-off.\n   - Keep #174's data path:\n     - background thumbnails and posters;\n     - streamed assets;\n     - the windowed Archive;\n     - patching only the touched cards;\n     - the cached library size.\n   - Glass sparingly and never on grid cards. No Zustand or TanStack Query.\n   - **Comments:**\n     - Default to none; one line where possible, four at most.\n     - Keep only race/ordering, security/sanitizing, Chromium/Electron/WebGPU/OS quirks, or a cross-file invariant.\n     - Delete restated names, narration, section labels, history, and TODOs without an issue.\n     - Lint directives, knip tags and license headers stay.\n     - Mascot engines, ingestion and LiquidGlass are out of scope unless a layer already moves them.\n   - **Tests:**\n     - Moved tests stay unchanged except their imports. New tests must meet SQU-132's keep bar.\n     - No sleeps, per-test timeouts, retries, Date.now/performance.now deltas, polling, or skips without a reason.\n   - **Verify:**\n     - Each PR lists the \"Hit every surface\" entries that applied.\n     - Full app via verify-inkling (liquid glass) plus preview (CSS fallback).\n     - Before/after screenshots, base vs branch.\n     - Keyboard and focus return for every Dialog, Tabs and Menu.\n     - `bun run check` once per layer.\n   - Rebase upper layers if a lower one changes. Never force-push a branch that isn't yours.\n   - **Stop and ask only if:**\n     - the gate fails;\n     - an AGENTS.md rule fights the work;\n     - visible behavior changes beyond parity;\n     - Base UI can't coexist with the glass canvas;\n     - something is destructive or touches the live library;\n     - CI is red for a reason that can't be pinned down.\n   - **Done when:**\n     - every child issue has a PR green on CI at its latest commit, linked, with the issue In Review;\n     - App.css is gone, and no UI file is a god file without a written reason;\n     - storage.mjs is split (SQU-125, PR #175, In Review);\n     - comments and tests follow the rules, and AGENTS.md carries them;\n     - docs match reality;\n     - a summary comment on SQU-124 lists every PR, test and comment counts before and after, anything skipped and why, and follow-ups.\n\n   **SQU-132 description**\n   - Move what is left in App.css to its owner: onboarding keyframes and GSAP selectors next to FirstRunOverlay, toast styling next to the Toaster. Then delete App.css.\n   - reader.css stays plain CSS. Move it next to ReaderView and point it at the shared tokens.\n   - No UI file over about 600 lines without a reason.\n   - Docs:\n     - rewrite the tech-stack styling row, and remove or justify Zustand/TanStack;\n     - design.md tokens to the real ones;\n     - a changelog line under Changed referencing SQU-124;\n     - rewrite, don't append.\n   - Update t3.json, knip.json and biome.jsonc if needed.\n   - Done when:\n     - App.css is gone and `bun run check` passes;\n     - onboarding plays through unchanged (screen order and mascot rhythm);\n     - the reader renders sanitized article HTML as before;\n     - there's a final walkthrough of every surface in the full app, with a short video for any motion.\n\n   **SQU-132 comment** (this wins)\n   - Onboarding (#173): move only its CSS and keyframes.\n   - tech-stack.md and design.md must describe the liquid glass layer:\n     - the WebGPU canvas;\n     - the `.glass`/`.css-glass` contract;\n     - the CSS fallback.\n   - **Test prune** across src/ and electron/:\n     - **Delete:** type-redundant, trivial, basic DOM, static-markup, mock-call mirrors, smoke, duplicate table rows, wall-clock/perf.\n     - **Keep:** extraction/sanitizing, embed allowlists, OCR scoring, queue leases/recovery, migrations/persistence, asset path containment/range requests, deep link/external-format parsing, ordering/race guarantees, liquidGlassShape, and any test added by a fix commit. Mark it `// regression: #NNN` if its name doesn't say so.\n     - Remove helpers and exports that only the deleted tests used, with no product-code change.\n     - Report before/after test counts and `bun test` time in the PR.\n   - **AGENTS.md:** add the comment and test rules to the Taste and Verifying sections, in its own voice. Rewrite the existing lines; no custom lint rules.\n\n   **AGENTS.md safety constraints (verbatim essentials)**\n   - \"Never `pkill -f`, `pgrep | kill`, or `kill` a PID you found by matching a name, path, or worktree string... Kill only a PID you captured at spawn, or the owner of your port after confirming it is your worktree (`Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort <port> -State Listen` and the `Win32_Process` command line on Windows).\"\n   - \"Never start a server against [the live library], never open it read-write, never clean it up.\"\n   - \"Never hardcode a localhost port, an absolute user path, or a machine specific model cache path into source or committed config.\"\n   - \"Never commit a database file, a model artifact, a downloaded embedding, or a benchmark output besides the two tracked files. Never commit a pairing secret, token, or full capture URL with real content.\"\n   - \"Never `Start-Sleep` (or any blocking wait) after launching a server.\"\n   - No calls home or analytics.\n   - Don't commit plans or scratch; keep scratch outside the worktree.\n   - Never commit PR-only screenshots; upload them to GitHub.\n   - PR body:\n     - Linear link at the top, then Problem and Fix.\n     - End with the model/harness line, then `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`.\n     - UI changes need before/after images.\n   - Commit messages end with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.\n   - Linear workflow:\n     - set In Progress;\n     - post progress comments;\n     - never rewrite descriptions;\n     - link the PR;\n     - move to In Review.\n   - Never use bare `git stash`.\n   - Register every PR with `mcp__t3-code__link_pull_request`.\n   - Entire hook: don't create checkpoints by hand.\n   - The user's email is only for identification; never send it anywhere.\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts**\n   - **Stack:** Electron, React 19, Vite 8, Tailwind v4 (no preflight), Base UI 1.9.0, Sonner toasts, TipTap note editor, GSAP, Biome, knip, tsc-rs, bun test.\n   - **Cascade:**\n     - Tailwind layers `theme, base, components, utilities`. Unlayered CSS beats utilities.\n     - Surface.css stays unlayered because `.glass[data-liquid]` must beat utilities (ZoomableImage uses `data-liquid:shadow-[...]!`).\n     - The `wide:` variant is `min-width: 781px` (`--breakpoint-wide`).\n     - Tailwind emits `max-[1120px]` before `max-[780px]` (verified in the built CSS), so the smaller breakpoint wins.\n   - `item.accent` is runtime-only (not persisted). Its values are now Tailwind classes (`bg-blue-soft`, `bg-yellow-soft`, `bg-green-soft`). LibraryCard uses `item.accent ?? \"bg-surface\"`.\n   - Lazy chunks emit their own CSS (RichNoteEditor.css becomes a separate chunk; Vite preloads it with the dynamic import).\n   - **Known local Windows-only check failures:**\n     - lint: 4 CRLF `.d.mts` format errors;\n     - bun test: the data-dir portable precedence test (path separators).\n   - PR #175 (SQU-125) is open against main. It touches storage.mjs and the `src/lib/notes.test.ts` comment at lines 26–30 (avoid editing there), but not storage.test.ts.\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections**\n\n   Worktree `C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8`, now on branch `squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss`, based on 16610f5. Nothing is committed yet for SQU-132.\n\n   - **`src/App.css`**: deleted (`git rm`). Its imports were removed from App.tsx.\n\n   - **`src/main.tsx`**: font imports added before `./index.css`:\n     ```ts\n     import \"@fontsource/libre-baskerville/400.css\";\n     import \"@fontsource/libre-baskerville/700.css\";\n     import \"@fontsource/libre-baskerville/400-italic.css\";\n     import \"@fontsource-variable/dm-sans/wght.css\";\n     import \"@fontsource/dm-mono/400.css\";\n     ```\n\n   - **`src/index.css`**\n     - Preflight comment rewritten to: \"No preflight: components were ported against browser defaults, and the few element resets they rely on live in base so utilities still win.\"\n     - Appended, unlayered:\n       - `@media (max-width:1120px){:root{--spacing-sidebar:220px}}`;\n       - the global `:focus-visible` outline (2px accent, offset 3px) for button/input/textarea/select/a/[tabindex];\n       - `@keyframes spin`;\n       - the prefers-reduced-motion global duration override.\n\n   - **`src/ui/Surface.css`**: comment is now `/* Unlayered, so it beats utilities on the same element; override with \\`!\\`. */`\n\n   - **`visually-hidden` → `sr-only`** in:\n     - SegmentedControl.tsx\n     - AddMenu.tsx\n     - ViewDock.tsx\n     - ArchivePanel.tsx\n     - ExtensionPairing.tsx\n     - SpacesSection.tsx\n\n   - **Accent values:**\n     - `useCapture.ts`: `paper-blue` → `bg-blue-soft`, `paper-yellow` → `bg-yellow-soft`.\n     - `libraryItem.ts`: `bg-yellow-soft`.\n     - `seed.ts`: `bg-green-soft`, `bg-yellow-soft`.\n     - `LibraryCard.tsx`: `: (item.accent ?? \"bg-surface\"),`.\n\n   - **`src/ui/IconButton.tsx`**: added `export const iconButtonClass = (size: keyof typeof sizes = \"md\") => cx(\"inline-grid place-items-center rounded-lg border border-transparent bg-transparent text-muted cursor-pointer transition-[background-color,color,border-color] duration-180 ease-[ease] hover:border-border hover:bg-surface hover:text-ink [&_svg]:block\", sizes[size]);`. IconButton now uses `cx(iconButtonClass(size), className)`.\n\n   - **`ShortcutsDialog.tsx`**: DialogClose uses `className={iconButtonClass(\"sm\")}` and imports from `../../ui/IconButton`.\n\n   - **`MascotHomeSlot.tsx`**: imports `cx` and uses `cx(\"h-11 flex-none origin-center overflow-hidden [transition:width_0.35s_cubic-bezier(0.2,0.8,0.2,1),opacity_0.3s_ease] [&_svg]:block [&_svg]:size-full\", isSearchFocused ? \"w-0 opacity-0\" : \"w-11\")` (was `.brand-mark`).\n\n   - **`LibraryStage.tsx`**\n     - The text-button became `cursor-pointer border-0 bg-transparent text-[13px] text-accent underline underline-offset-3`.\n     - LiquidGlass className: `absolute inset-0 z-0 overflow-hidden [&_.liquid-glass-canvas]:h-screen [&_.liquid-glass-canvas]:w-screen [&_.liquid-glass-content]:bg-(--stage-background)`, with a 3-line comment about the WebGPU canvas resize stall.\n\n   - **`LiquidGlass.tsx`**\n     - The content element's className is `\"liquid-glass-content absolute inset-0\"`.\n     - The canvas className is `\"liquid-glass-canvas absolute top-0 left-0 block size-full\"`.\n     - The comment now references LibraryStage instead of App.css.\n\n   - **`App.tsx`**\n     - Imports `cx` and `Toaster` from `./ui/Toaster`.\n     - Removed the `sonner` import and the `Cancel01Icon` import.\n     - Renders `<Toaster />`.\n     - `<main>` className:\n       ```tsx\n       cx(\n         \"relative flex h-screen min-h-0 w-auto min-w-0 flex-auto flex-col overflow-hidden pt-(--main-pad-top) pr-(--main-pad-x) pb-(--main-pad-bottom) pl-(--main-pad-x) transition-[padding] duration-300 ease-[cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1)] [--library-top:var(--main-pad-top)] [--main-pad-bottom:30px] [--main-pad-top:calc(4px_+_var(--spacing-titlebar))] [--main-pad-x:14px] [--stage-background:var(--color-canvas)]\",\n         \"wide:rounded-l-frame wide:border wide:border-r-0 wide:border-border wide:bg-frame wide:transition-[margin-left,padding] wide:[--stage-background:var(--color-frame)]\",\n         isSidebarOpen ? \"wide:ml-(--spacing-sidebar)\" : \"wide:ml-0\",\n         \"max-[1120px]:w-[calc(100vw_-_var(--spacing-sidebar))] max-[780px]:w-full max-[780px]:transition-none max-[780px]:[--library-top:42px] max-[780px]:[--main-pad-bottom:24px] max-[780px]:[--main-pad-top:12px] max-[780px]:[--main-pad-x:18px]\",\n       )\n       ```\n     - The library-header section is now `<section className=\"flex-none max-[780px]:pt-[30px]\"></section>`.\n\n   - **`Sidebar.tsx`** comment: \"...the library frame (App's <main>) slides over it.\"\n\n   - **New `src/ui/Toaster.tsx`**: wraps Sonner's Toaster with the same props (top-right, offset `{top:48,right:16}`, mobileOffset, dark, `richColors={false}`, closeButton, duration 5000, empty success/error icons, a Cancel01Icon close at size 12, containerAriaLabel \"Notifications\") and imports `./Toaster.css`.\n\n   - **New `src/ui/Toaster.css`**: the old App.css toast rules verbatim, minus 3 section-label comments.\n\n   - **AddMenu.css**: the `.add-button` rules appended (keeping the \"scale, not transform\" comment); the section-label comment dropped.\n\n   - **New `src/features/item-view/RichNoteEditor.css`**: all the `.note-editor*`, `.note-embedded*`, `.note-focus-editor*` and `.note-link*` rules verbatim (573 lines). They're kept as CSS because they style TipTap-generated HTML, and base rules leak into embedded mode (for example toolbar `min-width: 30px`). Imported by RichNoteEditor.tsx.\n\n   - **New `src/components/onboarding/onboarding.css`** (674 lines), imported by FirstRunOverlay.tsx.\n     - Contains the first-run, memory, kept, reads and crumb rules and their keyframes.\n     - `.first-run-crumb .breadcrumb-list` was renamed to `.first-run-crumb [data-slot=\"breadcrumb-list\"]`.\n     - Comments trimmed. The stage comment is now: \"The --fr-* scale is in stage pixels: FirstRunOverlay scales the stage with the window, so never animate its scale. --fr-dir is 1 going forward and -1 going back.\"\n     - Kept comments: the SplitText one, the caret, \"Runs once, so nothing repaints after the trail has lit.\", and \"KeptFloating owns transform...\".\n\n   - **`Breadcrumb.tsx`**: converted to Tailwind with `cx`.\n     - list: `m-0 flex list-none flex-wrap items-center gap-2 p-0 font-body text-[13px]/[1.4] text-muted`\n     - item: `inline-flex items-center gap-1.5`\n     - page: `text-accent`\n     - separator: `inline-flex opacity-80`\n     - Comment: \"coss ui's Breadcrumb: the same nav > ol > li structure and data-slot hooks. Only the parts inkling uses.\"\n\n   - **Comment repoints:**\n     - FirstRunOverlay: \"matches fr-stage-out in onboarding.css.\"\n     - MemoryMatch: \"in onboarding.css.\"\n     - LibraryCard and SettingsSheet: \"index.css's unlayered focus ring\".\n     - electron/main.mjs: \"body min-width in src/index.css\".\n\n   - **`knip.json`**: removed `ignoreDependencies` for the fontsource packages.\n\n   - **Test prune:**\n     - Deleted `src/components/ItemMedia.test.ts` and `src/components/mascot/inklingSkins.test.ts`.\n     - Dropped tests:\n       - **alive.test.ts:** 3 registration/smoke tests.\n       - **SearchOutline.test.ts:** 2 smoke tests.\n       - **previewMode.test.ts:** the hasPreviewQuery and env flags tests, and \"plain browser always uses seeds\".\n       - **keyboardShortcuts.test.ts:** 3 mapping tests. It keeps \"does not steal keys…\".\n       - **assetUrlCache.test.ts:** \"evicts old entries at the size limit\".\n       - **imageZoom.test.ts:** the wheel test.\n       - **noteMarkdown.test.ts:** \"round-trips headings…\".\n       - **readmeMascot.test.ts:** 3 static-markup tests.\n       - **notes.test.ts:** normalizeNoteBody.\n       - **libraryApi.test.ts:** 7 mock-mirror tests, plus their proxy command branches and imports.\n       - **electron/asset-response.test.ts:** \"unknown extensions fall back to a binary content type\".\n     - Unused imports removed via `biome check --write --unsafe`.\n     - Un-exported test-only helpers (still used internally): `fileExtensionLabel`, `formatFileSize`, `noteWordCount` in ItemMedia.tsx; `hasPreviewQuery`, `isPreviewBuildFlag`, `isDevFlag` in previewMode.ts.\n     - Result: before 324 tests in 40 files, 36.40s; after 284 tests in 38 files, 40.33s (noise; the slow electron/OCR suites are kept). 1 known Windows-only fail both times.\n\n   - **`AGENTS.md`**\n     - Verifying: the \"Test meaningful…\", \"Ingestion and background…\" and \"Background work is async…\" lines were rewritten into:\n       - the keep-bar line, with the regression marker;\n       - the \"Don't write tests the types already prove…\" line;\n       - the shortened ingestion line;\n       - the async line: no sleeps, per-test timeouts, retries, Date.now/performance.now deltas, polling loops, or skips without a reason.\n     - Taste: the \"Comments say why…\" line was rewritten to the default-no-comment rule (keep categories, one to four lines, deletion categories, and lint directives/knip tags/license headers stay).\n\n   - **`docs/tech-stack.md`**\n     - The Styling row now reads \"Tailwind CSS v4 utilities, Base UI headless primitives, and a WebGPU liquid glass layer\".\n     - Zustand and TanStack rows replaced by: \"UI state | React hooks per feature, composed in `App` | The renderer's state is small and local; library rows are patched by item id instead of cached and invalidated\".\n     - A new \"## Styling\" section before \"## Article extraction\" covers tokens, Base UI, where plain CSS is allowed, and the liquid glass contract (layoutsubtree canvas, HTML-in-Canvas, `.glass` vs `.css-glass`, `data-liquid`, the fallbacks, GPU cost, never on card surfaces).\n\n   - **`docs/design.md`**\n     - \"Materials and tokens\" rewritten with the real dark tokens from `src/index.css` (`@theme`): ground, surfaces, ink, accent, paper tints, Space colors, type, radii, glass.\n     - The composition line is now \"An open item replaces the library frame: its media sits on a dotted stage, with an inspector on the right.\"\n\n   - **`docs/product-behavior.md`**: new \"## Item view\" section before \"## Reading and writing\" (grow into the frame; dotted stage with zoom/pan/pixels; inspector with Info/Similar; action bar; delete only when archived; close only via Close/Escape; history via side buttons and Alt+Left/Right).\n\n   - **`docs/expanded-item-overlay.md`**: deleted (a stale pre-implementation spec). `docs/README.md` now says `- [design.md](design.md) — visual system.`\n\n   - **`docs/changelog.md`**: added at the top of Unreleased → Changed: \"- The interface is rebuilt on Tailwind CSS and Base UI primitives, split into feature folders with no visible change; tabs and menus now take one Tab stop and move with the arrow keys, and Escape in a menu closes only that menu (SQU-124)\".\n\n   - **Scratch helpers in `%TEMP%\\squ132`:**\n     - `split_css.py`\n     - `drop_tests.py` (removes test/describe blocks by name)\n   - **`%TEMP%\\squ131`:**\n     - Scripts: `composite.mjs`, `preview.ts`, `flight.ts`, `peek.ts`, `fullapp.ts`, `db.ts`.\n     - Shots: `full-before/`, `full-after/`, `before/`, `after/`.\n\n   - **Largest UI files, reasons for the PR:**\n     - App.tsx, 780 lines: composition root whose hook order carries App()'s ordering guarantees.\n     - ItemView.tsx, 721: verbatim GSAP flight.\n     - LibraryCard, 639, and ItemMedia, 630: per-kind card and media treatments.\n     - onboarding.css, 674: keyframe-driven screens.\n     - RichNoteEditor.css, 573.\n     - Mascot engine files are out of scope.\n     - electron/storage.mjs, 2462 lines: split in #175.\n\n4. **Errors and fixes**\n   - **The AddMenu block extraction was empty:** `index('.liquid-glass-canvas {')` matched the earlier `.library-stage .liquid-glass-canvas` rule. Fixed by searching for `'\\n.liquid-glass-canvas {'`.\n   - **The onboarding replacement assert failed:** the breadcrumb cut used `index(\".breadcrumb-list {\")`, which matched `.first-run-crumb .breadcrumb-list {` first and removed too much. Fixed with `index(\"\\n.breadcrumb-list {\") + 1`.\n   - **A sed edit to the python script inserted a literal newline in a string:** fixed with the Edit tool.\n   - **`grep --` broke the include flags:** the results were still usable.\n   - **Biome safe fixes didn't remove unused imports:** used `--unsafe`.\n\n5. **Problem Solving**\n   - **SQU-131:**\n     - Full-app pixel diffs confirmed timing-only.\n     - PR #181 is a draft, linked to the thread and to Linear, with a Linear comment posted.\n     - Remaining: mark it ready once CI is green and move SQU-131 to In Review.\n   - **#180:** CI green, marked ready; SQU-130 In Review.\n   - **SQU-132 status:**\n     - Typecheck and knip are clean after the CSS move and the prune.\n     - The build succeeded; the CSS ordering was verified.\n     - Lint shows only the 4 known CRLF errors.\n     - Still to do: visual verification, the remaining check parts (build:app, ingest:smoke, extension build), commit, and PR.\n\n6. **All user messages**\n   - The original `/goal` command (quoted above).\n   - \"[Request interrupted by user]\"\n   - `/goal clear`\n   - `/goal resume`\n   - \"Continue where you left off.\" (several times).\n   - Harness reminders asking for brief status updates. These are not requests.\n\n7. **Pending Tasks**\n   - **SQU-132:**\n     - Optional: move reader.css next to ReaderView (the issue says to move it next to ReaderView and use the tokens). ReaderView.tsx is at `src/ReaderView.tsx`, with `src/reader.css` beside it.\n     - Check t3.json and biome.jsonc for needed changes.\n     - Visual verification, base = SQU-131 commit 16610f5 vs branch:\n       - preview: library frame wide/narrow, sidebar slide, toasts, Breadcrumb/onboarding, note editor (embedded and focus), shortcuts dialog close button, card accents (notes/quotes), mascot home slot collapse;\n       - full app via verify-inkling: onboarding play-through (a short video for motion), reader with an article, note edit, toasts (archive undo), liquid glass stage.\n       - Keyboard/focus checks.\n     - Run `bun run check` parts: typecheck, extension and ingestion-shared typecheck, check:refs, bun test, knip, lint, build, build:app, ingest:smoke, extension build.\n     - Commit (Co-Authored-By line, `git commit -F file < /dev/null`), push, and open a draft PR against `squidlee/squ-131-stack-67-item-view-overlay`.\n       - Body: Linear link first, Problem, Fix, test counts (324→284 tests, 40→38 files, 36.4s→40.3s), god-file reasons, Hit every surface, Verification, before/after images, the model line, and the 🤖 line.\n     - Link the PR with the t3 tool and on Linear, post a Linear comment, mark ready when CI is green, and move SQU-132 to In Review.\n   - **SQU-131:** check #181 CI, mark ready, move to In Review.\n   - **Comment counts before (main) and after (branch)** for the SQU-124 summary, e.g. a script counting comment lines in src/ and electron/.\n   - **Final SQU-124 summary comment:**\n     - PRs #175 and #176–#182 (verify numbers);\n     - test counts and comment counts;\n     - skipped items: PdfViewer not folded onto Dialog; note editor and onboarding kept as co-located CSS; god-file reasons;\n     - follow-ups:\n       - the bench script is Linux-only and stale;\n       - the full-app archive-select issue;\n       - verify-inkling occlusion and toasts;\n       - Bun 1.4.4 vs 1.4.2;\n       - ui:smoke step 1 fails on base;\n       - toasts cover the Settings header tools;\n       - the PDF viewer's light header and the PDF.js worker failing in the unpackaged build;\n       - ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE leaks in the harness;\n       - the verify cdp `key()` helper lacks arrow keys;\n       - the Windows-only test/lint failures;\n       - the ReaderView CSS chunk is 190 kB (check);\n       - the RichNoteEditor `embedded` prop is always true (a simplification candidate).\n   - **Cleanup at the end.** Verify each command line first:\n     - Edge PID 24972 (:9400);\n     - branch Vite dev PID 4332 (:51205);\n     - vite preview bun PIDs 25612 and 32484 (ports 58561 and 58562; check owners);\n     - verify instances: `INKLING_VERIFY_NAME=squ131 INKLING_VERIFY_PORT=9336 ... cleanup` from the worktree, and `squ131base`/9337 from `%TEMP%\\squ126\\base`;\n     - `git worktree remove %TEMP%\\squ126\\base`.\n\n8. **Current Work**\n\n   I had just added the SQU-124 changelog line to `docs/changelog.md`, which finished the docs portion of SQU-132. The code moves, App.css deletion, test prune, AGENTS.md rules and docs rewrites are all in the working tree, uncommitted, on branch `squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss`. Typecheck and knip were clean after the code changes; bun test showed 284 tests with only the known Windows failure.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step**\n\n   Continue SQU-132 per the standing directive (\"Work until all are done; don't pause between layers\"):\n   1. Decide on and do the reader.css move next to ReaderView (the issue: \"Move it next to ReaderView and point it at the shared tokens\").\n   2. Check t3.json and biome.jsonc.\n   3. Rebuild, then do the preview and full-app visual verification against base 16610f5 (onboarding play-through video, reader, toasts, note editor, library frame/sidebar).\n   4. Run the check parts, commit, and open the SQU-132 draft PR against the SQU-131 branch.\n   5. Finish the SQU-131/132 Linear and PR states, then post the SQU-124 summary comment.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\chris\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-chris--t3-worktrees-inkling-t3-a1f541e8\\bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"13300c68-a226-49d6-ba46-b49cbfe436a4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:46:02.468Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":7},"turnOrigin":"sdk","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["76433fc7-af93-4f00-8078-64be2f9e1039"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
{"parentUuid":"13300c68-a226-49d6-ba46-b49cbfe436a4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\squ132\\drop_tests.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\squ132\\drop_tests.py","content":"\"\"\"Remove named test()/describe() blocks from a test file.\n\nusage: drop_tests.py FILE NAME [NAME...]\nEach NAME is the exact first argument string of a test( or describe( call.\n\"\"\"\nimport re\nimport sys\n\n\ndef block_end(s: str, start: int) -> int:\n    i = s.index(\"(\", start)\n    depth = 0\n    quote = None\n    while i < len(s):\n        ch = s[i]\n        if quote:\n            if ch == \"\\\\\":\n                i += 2\n                continue\n            if ch == quote:\n                quote = None\n        elif ch in \"\\\"'`\":\n            quote = ch\n        elif ch == \"(\":\n            depth += 1\n        elif ch == \")\":\n            depth -= 1\n            if depth == 0:\n                end = i + 1\n                if s[end : end + 1] == \";\":\n                    end += 1\n                if s[end : end + 1] == \"\\n\":\n                    end += 1\n                return end\n        i += 1\n    raise SystemExit(\"unbalanced\")\n\n\npath, *names = sys.argv[1:]\ns = open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\nfor name in names:\n    m = re.search(r\"^[ \\t]*(?:test|describe)(?:\\.each\\([^\\n]*?\\))?\\(\\s*\" + re.escape(json_name := '\"' + name + '\"'), s, re.M)\n    if not m:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"not found: {name}\")\n    start = m.start()\n    end = block_end(s, start)\n    # drop one blank line left behind\n    if s[end : end + 1] == \"\\n\" and (start == 0 or s[start - 2 : start] == \"\\n\\n\"):\n        end += 1\n    s = s[:start] + s[end:]\nopen(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\\n\").write(s)\n","numLines":52,"startLine":1,"totalLines":52}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\..\\..\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\squ132\\drop_tests.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cdc35da1-f008-453e-a5db-ae9dce685ddd","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:46:02.730Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chris\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\squ132\\\\drop_tests.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t\"\"\"Remove named test()/describe() blocks from a test file.\n2\t\n3\tusage: drop_tests.py FILE NAME [NAME...]\n4\tEach NAME is the exact first argument string of a test( or describe( call.\n5\t\"\"\"\n6\timport re\n7\timport sys\n8\t\n9\t\n10\tdef block_end(s: str, start: int) -> int:\n11\t    i = s.index(\"(\", start)\n12\t    depth = 0\n13\t    quote = None\n14\t    while i < len(s):\n15\t        ch = s[i]\n16\t        if quote:\n17\t            if ch == \"\\\\\":\n18\t                i += 2\n19\t                continue\n20\t            if ch == quote:\n21\t                quote = None\n22\t        elif ch in \"\\\"'`\":\n23\t            quote = ch\n24\t        elif ch == \"(\":\n25\t            depth += 1\n26\t        elif ch == \")\":\n27\t            depth -= 1\n28\t            if depth == 0:\n29\t                end = i + 1\n30\t                if s[end : end + 1] == \";\":\n31\t                    end += 1\n32\t                if s[end : end + 1] == \"\\n\":\n33\t                    end += 1\n34\t                return end\n35\t        i += 1\n36\t    raise SystemExit(\"unbalanced\")\n37\t\n38\t\n39\tpath, *names = sys.argv[1:]\n40\ts = open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\n41\tfor name in names:\n42\t    m = re.search(r\"^[ \\t]*(?:test|describe)(?:\\.each\\([^\\n]*?\\))?\\(\\s*\" + re.escape(json_name := '\"' + name + '\"'), s, re.M)\n43\t    if not m:\n44\t        raise SystemExit(f\"not found: {name}\")\n45\t    start = m.start()\n46\t    end = block_end(s, start)\n47\t    # drop one blank line left behind\n48\t    if s[end : end + 1] == \"\\n\" and (start == 0 or s[start - 2 : start] == \"\\n\\n\"):\n49\t        end += 1\n50\t    s = s[:start] + s[end:]\n51\topen(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\\n\").write(s)\n52\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
{"parentUuid":"cdc35da1-f008-453e-a5db-ae9dce685ddd","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8\\knip.json","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8\\knip.json","content":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://unpkg.com/knip@6/schema.json\",\n  \"workspaces\": {\n    \".\": {\n      \"entry\": [\n        \"src/**/*.test.ts\",\n        \"benchmarks/**/*.smoke.ts\",\n        \"electron/model-manifest.json\",\n        \"electron/**/*.d.mts\",\n        \"electron/**/*.test.ts\",\n        \"electron/preload.cjs\"\n      ],\n      \"project\": [\"src/**/*\", \"benchmarks/harness/**/*\", \"electron/**/*\"],\n      \"ignore\": [\"src/bun-test.d.ts\", \"src/components/GradualBlur/**\"]\n    },\n    \"extension\": {\n      \"entry\": [\"src/options.ts\", \"src/background.ts\", \"src/**/*.test.ts\"]\n    },\n    \"packages/*\": {}\n  }\n}\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}},"displayPath":"knip.json"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"73e78e02-a58a-4ec8-b1bd-7b09f2b2eb8a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:46:02.730Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chris\\\\.t3\\\\worktrees\\\\inkling\\\\t3-a1f541e8\\\\knip.json\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t{\n2\t  \"$schema\": \"https://unpkg.com/knip@6/schema.json\",\n3\t  \"workspaces\": {\n4\t    \".\": {\n5\t      \"entry\": [\n6\t        \"src/**/*.test.ts\",\n7\t        \"benchmarks/**/*.smoke.ts\",\n8\t        \"electron/model-manifest.json\",\n9\t        \"electron/**/*.d.mts\",\n10\t        \"electron/**/*.test.ts\",\n11\t        \"electron/preload.cjs\"\n12\t      ],\n13\t      \"project\": [\"src/**/*\", \"benchmarks/harness/**/*\", \"electron/**/*\"],\n14\t      \"ignore\": [\"src/bun-test.d.ts\", \"src/components/GradualBlur/**\"]\n15\t    },\n16\t    \"extension\": {\n17\t      \"entry\": [\"src/options.ts\", \"src/background.ts\", \"src/**/*.test.ts\"]\n18\t    },\n19\t    \"packages/*\": {}\n20\t  }\n21\t}\n22\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
{"parentUuid":"73e78e02-a58a-4ec8-b1bd-7b09f2b2eb8a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8\\src\\components\\FirstRunOverlay.tsx","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8\\src\\components\\FirstRunOverlay.tsx","content":"import { useEffect, useRef, useState, type CSSProperties } from \"react\";\nimport {\n  Breadcrumb,\n  BreadcrumbItem,\n  BreadcrumbList,\n  BreadcrumbPage,\n  BreadcrumbSeparator,\n} from \"./Breadcrumb\";\nimport { prefersReducedMotion } from \"./mascot/mascotStore\";\nimport { KeptFloating } from \"./onboarding/KeptFloating\";\nimport { MemoryMatch } from \"./onboarding/MemoryMatch\";\nimport { OnboardingMascot } from \"./onboarding/OnboardingMascot\";\nimport { preloadOnboardingPhotos } from \"./onboarding/onboardingMedia\";\nimport { ReadsPictures } from \"./onboarding/ReadsPictures\";\nimport { SplitText } from \"./onboarding/SplitText\";\nimport \"./onboarding/onboarding.css\";\n\n/**\n * Every screen is drawn on a 960x540 stage that keeps a fixed share of the\n * window: 1:1 at 1280x720 (or 1280x800), smaller below that, larger above it\n * up to a cap (about 1080p), past which more window only adds margin.\n */\nconst STAGE_FIT_WIDTH = 1280;\nconst STAGE_FIT_HEIGHT = 720;\nconst MAX_STAGE_SCALE = 1.35;\nconst LAST_SCREEN = 4;\n/**\n * Drawn size of the big cropped mascot at stage scale 1; the body is about 63% of it.\n * Its centre sits 0.2 of this from the window's side and bottom edges. The body\n * never shrinks below 0.237 of it, so the blob keeps bleeding off both edges\n * however it breathes and turns.\n */\nconst MASCOT_SIZE = 860;\n/** Eyes stay turned toward each screen's text (yaw + is right, pitch + is up). */\nconst WELCOME_LOOK = { yaw: -15, pitch: 24 };\nconst FAREWELL_LOOK = { yaw: 26, pitch: 12 };\n/** The big mascots run at this rate (1.8x slower), so they stay calm beside the text. */\nconst MASCOT_SPEED = 0.55;\n/** How long a screen takes to leave before the next one comes in; matches fr-stage-out in onboarding.css. */\nconst LEAVE_MS = 320;\n/**\n * When each screen's headline starts, in seconds. Screens whose demo opens\n * the scene hold the headline back; the rest of the copy follows it.\n */\nconst HEADLINE_DELAY = [0.15, 0.2, 0.45, 0.45, 0.15];\n\nconst welcomeFaces = [\"neutre\", \"curieux\", \"heureux\", \"attentif\"] as const;\nconst farewellFaces = [\"heureux\", \"neutre\", \"fier\", \"timide\"] as const;\n\nfunction stageScale() {\n  return Math.min(\n    MAX_STAGE_SCALE,\n    window.innerWidth / STAGE_FIT_WIDTH,\n    window.innerHeight / STAGE_FIT_HEIGHT,\n  );\n}\n\nexport function FirstRunOverlay({ onFinish }: { onFinish: () => void }) {\n  const [screen, setScreen] = useState(0);\n  const [scale, setScale] = useState(stageScale);\n  /** Set while the current screen plays its exit: 1 forward, -1 back, 0 closing. */\n  const [leaving, setLeaving] = useState<number | null>(null);\n  /** Which way the last move went, so the next screen comes in from that side. */\n  const [direction, setDirection] = useState(1);\n  const leaveTimer = useRef(0);\n\n  useEffect(() => () => window.clearTimeout(leaveTimer.current), []);\n\n  // Plays the current screen's exit, then lands on `next` (or closes the welcome).\n  const go = (next: number | \"close\") => {\n    if (leaving !== null) return;\n    const step = next === \"close\" ? 0 : next > screen ? 1 : -1;\n    const land = () => {\n      setLeaving(null);\n      if (next === \"close\") onFinish();\n      else {\n        setDirection(step);\n        setScreen(next);\n      }\n    };\n    if (prefersReducedMotion()) return land();\n    setLeaving(step);\n    leaveTimer.current = window.setTimeout(land, LEAVE_MS);\n  };\n  const goRef = useRef(go);\n  goRef.current = go;\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const update = () => setScale(stageScale());\n    const onKeyDown = (event: KeyboardEvent) => {\n      if (event.key === \"Escape\") goRef.current(\"close\");\n    };\n    window.addEventListener(\"resize\", update);\n    window.addEventListener(\"keydown\", onKeyDown);\n    return () => {\n      window.removeEventListener(\"resize\", update);\n      window.removeEventListener(\"keydown\", onKeyDown);\n    };\n  }, []);\n\n  // First launch keeps the window hidden until this screen has painted, and\n  // the later screens' photos decode meanwhile so none of them pop in.\n  useEffect(() => {\n    preloadOnboardingPhotos();\n    let frame = requestAnimationFrame(() => {\n      frame = requestAnimationFrame(\n        () => void window.inkling?.windowControls.ready().catch(() => null),\n      );\n    });\n    return () => cancelAnimationFrame(frame);\n  }, []);\n\n  const advance = () => go(screen === LAST_SCREEN ? \"close\" : screen + 1);\n\n  const actions = (style: CSSProperties) => (\n    <div className=\"first-run-actions\" style={style}>\n      <button type=\"button\" className=\"first-run-primary\" onClick={advance}>\n        {screen === LAST_SCREEN ? \"Open my library\" : \"Continue\"}\n      </button>\n      {screen > 0 ? (\n        <button type=\"button\" className=\"first-run-quiet\" onClick={() => go(screen - 1)}>\n          Back\n        </button>\n      ) : null}\n      <button type=\"button\" className=\"first-run-quiet\" onClick={() => go(\"close\")}>\n        Skip\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  );\n\n  const mascotSize = MASCOT_SIZE * scale;\n\n  return (\n    <div\n      className={leaving === 0 ? \"first-run-overlay is-closing\" : \"first-run-overlay\"}\n      role=\"dialog\"\n      aria-modal=\"true\"\n      aria-label=\"Welcome to inkling\"\n    >\n      {/* The big mascot hangs off the window's corner, not the stage's, so it\n          stays cropped by the window edge at any size. */}\n      {screen === 0 ? (\n        <OnboardingMascot\n          key=\"welcome\"\n          size={mascotSize}\n          faces={welcomeFaces}\n          look={WELCOME_LOOK}\n          speed={MASCOT_SPEED}\n          side=\"right\"\n          leaving={leaving !== null}\n          style={{ right: -0.3 * mascotSize, bottom: -0.3 * mascotSize }}\n        />\n      ) : null}\n      {screen === LAST_SCREEN ? (\n        <OnboardingMascot\n          key=\"farewell\"\n          size={mascotSize}\n          faces={farewellFaces}\n          look={FAREWELL_LOOK}\n          speed={MASCOT_SPEED}\n          side=\"left\"\n          leaving={leaving !== null}\n          style={{ left: -0.3 * mascotSize, bottom: -0.3 * mascotSize }}\n        />\n      ) : null}\n\n      <div\n        key={screen}\n        className={leaving === null ? \"first-run-stage\" : \"first-run-stage is-leaving\"}\n        style={\n          {\n            transform: `translate(-50%, -50%) scale(${scale})`,\n            \"--fr-dir\": leaving === null ? direction : leaving,\n            \"--fr-copy-delay\": `${HEADLINE_DELAY[screen] + 0.5}s`,\n          } as CSSProperties\n        }\n      >\n        {screen === 0 ? (\n          <>\n            <SplitText\n              text=\"Drop something in.\"\n              className=\"first-run-headline\"\n              style={{ left: 40, top: 128 }}\n              delay={HEADLINE_DELAY[0]}\n            />\n            <p className=\"first-run-body\" style={{ left: 40, top: 214 }}>\n              Paste a link, drop in a file, or grab a screenshot.\n              <br />\n              It&apos;s kept the moment it lands. No folders to pick.\n            </p>\n            <div className=\"first-run-keys\" style={{ left: 40, top: 300 }}>\n              <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>\n              <kbd>V</kbd>\n              <span>works anywhere in inkling</span>\n            </div>\n            {actions({ left: 40, top: 362 })}\n          </>\n        ) : null}\n\n        {screen === 1 ? (\n          <>\n            <KeptFloating />\n            <SplitText\n              text=\"Kept as it came.\"\n              className=\"first-run-headline is-centered\"\n              style={{ top: 137 }}\n              delay={HEADLINE_DELAY[1]}\n            />\n            <p className=\"first-run-body is-centered\" style={{ top: 222 }}>\n              Articles, photos, PDFs, quotes, notes and posts each get\n              <br />\n              their own card, right away. Reading and indexing happen\n              <br />\n              quietly while you keep going.\n            </p>\n            {actions({ top: 350, left: 0, right: 0, justifyContent: \"center\" })}\n          </>\n        ) : null}\n\n        {screen === 2 ? (\n          <>\n            <MemoryMatch />\n            <SplitText\n              text=\"Half a memory is enough.\"\n              className=\"first-run-headline is-centered\"\n              style={{ top: 326 }}\n              delay={HEADLINE_DELAY[2]}\n            />\n            <p className=\"first-run-body is-centered\" style={{ top: 408 }}>\n              Describe it the way it comes back to you. Search runs on this\n              <br />\n              computer, so nothing you save leaves it.\n            </p>\n            {actions({ top: 492, left: 0, right: 0, justifyContent: \"center\" })}\n          </>\n        ) : null}\n\n        {screen === 3 ? (\n          <>\n            <ReadsPictures />\n            <SplitText\n              text=\"It reads your pictures, too.\"\n              className=\"first-run-headline is-wrapped\"\n              style={{ left: 24, top: 76, width: 440 }}\n              delay={HEADLINE_DELAY[3]}\n            />\n            <p className=\"first-run-body\" style={{ left: 24, top: 233 }}>\n              Words inside screenshots, photos and PDFs are\n              <br />\n              searchable. Remember one word, find the whole\n              <br />\n              thing. All on this computer.\n            </p>\n            <div className=\"first-run-keys\" style={{ left: 24, top: 352 }}>\n              <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>\n              <kbd>K</kbd>\n              <span>to search from anywhere</span>\n            </div>\n            {actions({ left: 24, top: 414 })}\n          </>\n        ) : null}\n\n        {screen === LAST_SCREEN ? (\n          <>\n            <SplitText\n              text=\"It's all yours.\"\n              className=\"first-run-headline\"\n              style={{ left: 400, top: 116 }}\n              delay={HEADLINE_DELAY[4]}\n            />\n            <p className=\"first-run-body\" style={{ left: 400, top: 202 }}>\n              Your library lives on this computer, not in an\n              <br />\n              account. Export a full copy whenever you like.\n              <br />\n              inkling only goes online to fetch the links you save.\n            </p>\n            <Breadcrumb className=\"first-run-crumb\" style={{ left: 400, top: 322 }}>\n              <BreadcrumbList>\n                <BreadcrumbItem>Settings</BreadcrumbItem>\n                <BreadcrumbSeparator />\n                <BreadcrumbItem>Data</BreadcrumbItem>\n                <BreadcrumbSeparator />\n                <BreadcrumbItem>\n                  <BreadcrumbPage>Export a copy</BreadcrumbPage>\n                </BreadcrumbItem>\n              </BreadcrumbList>\n            </Breadcrumb>\n            {actions({ left: 400, top: 378 })}\n          </>\n        ) : null}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n","numLines":296,"startLine":1,"totalLines":296}},"displayPath":"src\\components\\FirstRunOverlay.tsx"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4b39bbd0-d3f7-425a-a197-29678ab76294","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:46:02.730Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chris\\\\.t3\\\\worktrees\\\\inkling\\\\t3-a1f541e8\\\\src\\\\components\\\\FirstRunOverlay.tsx\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\timport { useEffect, useRef, useState, type CSSProperties } from \"react\";\n2\timport {\n3\t  Breadcrumb,\n4\t  BreadcrumbItem,\n5\t  BreadcrumbList,\n6\t  BreadcrumbPage,\n7\t  BreadcrumbSeparator,\n8\t} from \"./Breadcrumb\";\n9\timport { prefersReducedMotion } from \"./mascot/mascotStore\";\n10\timport { KeptFloating } from \"./onboarding/KeptFloating\";\n11\timport { MemoryMatch } from \"./onboarding/MemoryMatch\";\n12\timport { OnboardingMascot } from \"./onboarding/OnboardingMascot\";\n13\timport { preloadOnboardingPhotos } from \"./onboarding/onboardingMedia\";\n14\timport { ReadsPictures } from \"./onboarding/ReadsPictures\";\n15\timport { SplitText } from \"./onboarding/SplitText\";\n16\timport \"./onboarding/onboarding.css\";\n17\t\n18\t/**\n19\t * Every screen is drawn on a 960x540 stage that keeps a fixed share of the\n20\t * window: 1:1 at 1280x720 (or 1280x800), smaller below that, larger above it\n21\t * up to a cap (about 1080p), past which more window only adds margin.\n22\t */\n23\tconst STAGE_FIT_WIDTH = 1280;\n24\tconst STAGE_FIT_HEIGHT = 720;\n25\tconst MAX_STAGE_SCALE = 1.35;\n26\tconst LAST_SCREEN = 4;\n27\t/**\n28\t * Drawn size of the big cropped mascot at stage scale 1; the body is about 63% of it.\n29\t * Its centre sits 0.2 of this from the window's side and bottom edges. The body\n30\t * never shrinks below 0.237 of it, so the blob keeps bleeding off both edges\n31\t * however it breathes and turns.\n32\t */\n33\tconst MASCOT_SIZE = 860;\n34\t/** Eyes stay turned toward each screen's text (yaw + is right, pitch + is up). */\n35\tconst WELCOME_LOOK = { yaw: -15, pitch: 24 };\n36\tconst FAREWELL_LOOK = { yaw: 26, pitch: 12 };\n37\t/** The big mascots run at this rate (1.8x slower), so they stay calm beside the text. */\n38\tconst MASCOT_SPEED = 0.55;\n39\t/** How long a screen takes to leave before the next one comes in; matches fr-stage-out in onboarding.css. */\n40\tconst LEAVE_MS = 320;\n41\t/**\n42\t * When each screen's headline starts, in seconds. Screens whose demo opens\n43\t * the scene hold the headline back; the rest of the copy follows it.\n44\t */\n45\tconst HEADLINE_DELAY = [0.15, 0.2, 0.45, 0.45, 0.15];\n46\t\n47\tconst welcomeFaces = [\"neutre\", \"curieux\", \"heureux\", \"attentif\"] as const;\n48\tconst farewellFaces = [\"heureux\", \"neutre\", \"fier\", \"timide\"] as const;\n49\t\n50\tfunction stageScale() {\n51\t  return Math.min(\n52\t    MAX_STAGE_SCALE,\n53\t    window.innerWidth / STAGE_FIT_WIDTH,\n54\t    window.innerHeight / STAGE_FIT_HEIGHT,\n55\t  );\n56\t}\n57\t\n58\texport function FirstRunOverlay({ onFinish }: { onFinish: () => void }) {\n59\t  const [screen, setScreen] = useState(0);\n60\t  const [scale, setScale] = useState(stageScale);\n61\t  /** Set while the current screen plays its exit: 1 forward, -1 back, 0 closing. */\n62\t  const [leaving, setLeaving] = useState<number | null>(null);\n63\t  /** Which way the last move went, so the next screen comes in from that side. */\n64\t  const [direction, setDirection] = useState(1);\n65\t  const leaveTimer = useRef(0);\n66\t\n67\t  useEffect(() => () => window.clearTimeout(leaveTimer.current), []);\n68\t\n69\t  // Plays the current screen's exit, then lands on `next` (or closes the welcome).\n70\t  const go = (next: number | \"close\") => {\n71\t    if (leaving !== null) return;\n72\t    const step = next === \"close\" ? 0 : next > screen ? 1 : -1;\n73\t    const land = () => {\n74\t      setLeaving(null);\n75\t      if (next === \"close\") onFinish();\n76\t      else {\n77\t        setDirection(step);\n78\t        setScreen(next);\n79\t      }\n80\t    };\n81\t    if (prefersReducedMotion()) return land();\n82\t    setLeaving(step);\n83\t    leaveTimer.current = window.setTimeout(land, LEAVE_MS);\n84\t  };\n85\t  const goRef = useRef(go);\n86\t  goRef.current = go;\n87\t\n88\t  useEffect(() => {\n89\t    const update = () => setScale(stageScale());\n90\t    const onKeyDown = (event: KeyboardEvent) => {\n91\t      if (event.key === \"Escape\") goRef.current(\"close\");\n92\t    };\n93\t    window.addEventListener(\"resize\", update);\n94\t    window.addEventListener(\"keydown\", onKeyDown);\n95\t    return () => {\n96\t      window.removeEventListener(\"resize\", update);\n97\t      window.removeEventListener(\"keydown\", onKeyDown);\n98\t    };\n99\t  }, []);\n100\t\n101\t  // First launch keeps the window hidden until this screen has painted, and\n102\t  // the later screens' photos decode meanwhile so none of them pop in.\n103\t  useEffect(() => {\n104\t    preloadOnboardingPhotos();\n105\t    let frame = requestAnimationFrame(() => {\n106\t      frame = requestAnimationFrame(\n107\t        () => void window.inkling?.windowControls.ready().catch(() => null),\n108\t      );\n109\t    });\n110\t    return () => cancelAnimationFrame(frame);\n111\t  }, []);\n112\t\n113\t  const advance = () => go(screen === LAST_SCREEN ? \"close\" : screen + 1);\n114\t\n115\t  const actions = (style: CSSProperties) => (\n116\t    <div className=\"first-run-actions\" style={style}>\n117\t      <button type=\"button\" className=\"first-run-primary\" onClick={advance}>\n118\t        {screen === LAST_SCREEN ? \"Open my library\" : \"Continue\"}\n119\t      </button>\n120\t      {screen > 0 ? (\n121\t        <button type=\"button\" className=\"first-run-quiet\" onClick={() => go(screen - 1)}>\n122\t          Back\n123\t        </button>\n124\t      ) : null}\n125\t      <button type=\"button\" className=\"first-run-quiet\" onClick={() => go(\"close\")}>\n126\t        Skip\n127\t      </button>\n128\t    </div>\n129\t  );\n130\t\n131\t  const mascotSize = MASCOT_SIZE * scale;\n132\t\n133\t  return (\n134\t    <div\n135\t      className={leaving === 0 ? \"first-run-overlay is-closing\" : \"first-run-overlay\"}\n136\t      role=\"dialog\"\n137\t      aria-modal=\"true\"\n138\t      aria-label=\"Welcome to inkling\"\n139\t    >\n140\t      {/* The big mascot hangs off the window's corner, not the stage's, so it\n141\t          stays cropped by the window edge at any size. */}\n142\t      {screen === 0 ? (\n143\t        <OnboardingMascot\n144\t          key=\"welcome\"\n145\t          size={mascotSize}\n146\t          faces={welcomeFaces}\n147\t          look={WELCOME_LOOK}\n148\t          speed={MASCOT_SPEED}\n149\t          side=\"right\"\n150\t          leaving={leaving !== null}\n151\t          style={{ right: -0.3 * mascotSize, bottom: -0.3 * mascotSize }}\n152\t        />\n153\t      ) : null}\n154\t      {screen === LAST_SCREEN ? (\n155\t        <OnboardingMascot\n156\t          key=\"farewell\"\n157\t          size={mascotSize}\n158\t          faces={farewellFaces}\n159\t          look={FAREWELL_LOOK}\n160\t          speed={MASCOT_SPEED}\n161\t          side=\"left\"\n162\t          leaving={leaving !== null}\n163\t          style={{ left: -0.3 * mascotSize, bottom: -0.3 * mascotSize }}\n164\t        />\n165\t      ) : null}\n166\t\n167\t      <div\n168\t        key={screen}\n169\t        className={leaving === null ? \"first-run-stage\" : \"first-run-stage is-leaving\"}\n170\t        style={\n171\t          {\n172\t            transform: `translate(-50%, -50%) scale(${scale})`,\n173\t            \"--fr-dir\": leaving === null ? direction : leaving,\n174\t            \"--fr-copy-delay\": `${HEADLINE_DELAY[screen] + 0.5}s`,\n175\t          } as CSSProperties\n176\t        }\n177\t      >\n178\t        {screen === 0 ? (\n179\t          <>\n180\t            <SplitText\n181\t              text=\"Drop something in.\"\n182\t              className=\"first-run-headline\"\n183\t              style={{ left: 40, top: 128 }}\n184\t              delay={HEADLINE_DELAY[0]}\n185\t            />\n186\t            <p className=\"first-run-body\" style={{ left: 40, top: 214 }}>\n187\t              Paste a link, drop in a file, or grab a screenshot.\n188\t              <br />\n189\t              It&apos;s kept the moment it lands. No folders to pick.\n190\t            </p>\n191\t            <div className=\"first-run-keys\" style={{ left: 40, top: 300 }}>\n192\t              <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>\n193\t              <kbd>V</kbd>\n194\t              <span>works anywhere in inkling</span>\n195\t            </div>\n196\t            {actions({ left: 40, top: 362 })}\n197\t          </>\n198\t        ) : null}\n199\t\n200\t        {screen === 1 ? (\n201\t          <>\n202\t            <KeptFloating />\n203\t            <SplitText\n204\t              text=\"Kept as it came.\"\n205\t              className=\"first-run-headline is-centered\"\n206\t              style={{ top: 137 }}\n207\t              delay={HEADLINE_DELAY[1]}\n208\t            />\n209\t            <p className=\"first-run-body is-centered\" style={{ top: 222 }}>\n210\t              Articles, photos, PDFs, quotes, notes and posts each get\n211\t              <br />\n212\t              their own card, right away. Reading and indexing happen\n213\t              <br />\n214\t              quietly while you keep going.\n215\t            </p>\n216\t            {actions({ top: 350, left: 0, right: 0, justifyContent: \"center\" })}\n217\t          </>\n218\t        ) : null}\n219\t\n220\t        {screen === 2 ? (\n221\t          <>\n222\t            <MemoryMatch />\n223\t            <SplitText\n224\t              text=\"Half a memory is enough.\"\n225\t              className=\"first-run-headline is-centered\"\n226\t              style={{ top: 326 }}\n227\t              delay={HEADLINE_DELAY[2]}\n228\t            />\n229\t            <p className=\"first-run-body is-centered\" style={{ top: 408 }}>\n230\t              Describe it the way it comes back to you. Search runs on this\n231\t              <br />\n232\t              computer, so nothing you save leaves it.\n233\t            </p>\n234\t            {actions({ top: 492, left: 0, right: 0, justifyContent: \"center\" })}\n235\t          </>\n236\t        ) : null}\n237\t\n238\t        {screen === 3 ? (\n239\t          <>\n240\t            <ReadsPictures />\n241\t            <SplitText\n242\t              text=\"It reads your pictures, too.\"\n243\t              className=\"first-run-headline is-wrapped\"\n244\t              style={{ left: 24, top: 76, width: 440 }}\n245\t              delay={HEADLINE_DELAY[3]}\n246\t            />\n247\t            <p className=\"first-run-body\" style={{ left: 24, top: 233 }}>\n248\t              Words inside screenshots, photos and PDFs are\n249\t              <br />\n250\t              searchable. Remember one word, find the whole\n251\t              <br />\n252\t              thing. All on this computer.\n253\t            </p>\n254\t            <div className=\"first-run-keys\" style={{ left: 24, top: 352 }}>\n255\t              <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>\n256\t              <kbd>K</kbd>\n257\t              <span>to search from anywhere</span>\n258\t            </div>\n259\t            {actions({ left: 24, top: 414 })}\n260\t          </>\n261\t        ) : null}\n262\t\n263\t        {screen === LAST_SCREEN ? (\n264\t          <>\n265\t            <SplitText\n266\t              text=\"It's all yours.\"\n267\t              className=\"first-run-headline\"\n268\t              style={{ left: 400, top: 116 }}\n269\t              delay={HEADLINE_DELAY[4]}\n270\t            />\n271\t            <p className=\"first-run-body\" style={{ left: 400, top: 202 }}>\n272\t              Your library lives on this computer, not in an\n273\t              <br />\n274\t              account. Export a full copy whenever you like.\n275\t              <br />\n276\t              inkling only goes online to fetch the links you save.\n277\t            </p>\n278\t            <Breadcrumb className=\"first-run-crumb\" style={{ left: 400, top: 322 }}>\n279\t              <BreadcrumbList>\n280\t                <BreadcrumbItem>Settings</BreadcrumbItem>\n281\t                <BreadcrumbSeparator />\n282\t                <BreadcrumbItem>Data</BreadcrumbItem>\n283\t                <BreadcrumbSeparator />\n284\t                <BreadcrumbItem>\n285\t                  <BreadcrumbPage>Export a copy</BreadcrumbPage>\n286\t                </BreadcrumbItem>\n287\t              </BreadcrumbList>\n288\t            </Breadcrumb>\n289\t            {actions({ left: 400, top: 378 })}\n290\t          </>\n291\t        ) : null}\n292\t      </div>\n293\t    </div>\n294\t  );\n295\t}\n296\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-a1f541e8","sessionId":"bf5ac5c7-e575-44db-b623-8a1386058030","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"squidlee/squ-132-stack-77-onboarding-reader-cleanup-delete-appcss","slug":"starry-painting-spark"}
