{"parentUuid":"e68d03c5-7fa7-4dea-98f1-48e1e1e84f81","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQZcCG4A846MBFHGBQZZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm planning full-app verification for SQU-132, starting with seeding an article. Rather than relying on a flaky real network fetch, I think serving an article locally via a tiny bun server on an ephemeral port would let me capture a deterministic, offline URL for testing.\n\nBeyond the article, I need to check note creation and editing through the embedded RichNoteEditor, archive-with-undo toast behavior, and the fresh-launch onboarding flow — since an empty scratch dir auto-triggers onboarding. For onboarding I'll record a short screencast via CDP's Page.startScreencast and assemble frames into video, assuming ffmpeg is available; I'll just capture the branch version rather than both.\n\nMy setup steps: clean up old squ131/squ131base verify instances, detach-checkout the base commit in its worktree (confirming it's clean and checking if package.json differs from the current commit before deciding whether a fresh bun install is needed), build both app versions, then launch them as squ132 and squ132base on separate ports for comparison.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_read_input_tokens":93472,"output_tokens":846,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":628},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2836,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":846,"cache_read_input_tokens":93472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2836},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":